const IDX=[{"title": "Renown", "url": "rules-renown.html", "text": "Renown\n A turn-based strategy game of empire building, diplomacy, and domain mastery.\n"}, {"title": "Introduction", "url": "rules-introduction.html", "text": "Introduction\nWithin the Realm, Empires expand, specialize, confer, and when diplomacy fails\u2014battle. You will lead your humble Province to greatness. Settle new Villages and Expand them, build your economy, and negotiate your way to victory. Will your religion dominate the Realm? Will your economy grow until your wealth is undeniable? Can you build a world wonder? Can you extort your way to victory? Pick your Faction, command your Domain, and pursue your Craft in this political grand strategy, where every action you attempt can be endorsed or condemned by your allies and other players.\nGame Synopsis\nRenown is a turn-based political strategy game for 1\u20137 players (3+ preferred) set in a medieval world of competing lords. Each player controls a growing empire \u2014 Settlements, Armies, and Holdings \u2014 but the game&#x27;s central tension isn&#x27;t military. It&#x27;s political.\nEvery action you want to take has to survive a vote. When you move your Army, build a road, or sabotage a rival, every other player at the table gets to spend political Influence to support or bury it. The strength of your relationships, the Alliances you&#x27;ve built, and the favors you&#x27;re owed decide whether "}, {"title": "Reading These Rules", "url": "rules-reading-these-rules.html", "text": "Reading These Rules\nA few conventions make every rule in this book read the same way:\n\nmay marks something optional. If a rule doesn&#x27;t say may, it&#x27;s mandatory.\ncan&#x27;t and doesn&#x27;t are hard stops (see Core Principle 2).\nEffects are written by when they apply: While X is always on; When X / At X happens once, at that moment; an action&#x27;s Cost / Effect / Endorsed happens when you take the action.\nLimits are written by window: At the Start of the Empire Phase happens once, in that step; Each &lt;Phase&gt; happens every time that phase does; Once per &lt;Phase&gt; can be used once, only during that phase; Once per turn can be used once, in any phase \u2014 a trigger such as when an Army ends a Move action fires in whichever phase the Move happens.\nChoose one: marks a set of options from which you pick exactly one.\nYou and your mean the player whose Holding, Infrastructure, Faction or Standing it is. Anything targeting you also covers what you own \u2014 your Settlements, Armies and Holdings.\nInfluence +X gives you X Influence tokens in the Empire Phase, unless it names another time. Authority \u00b1X changes an Envoy&#x27;s Authority while it&#x27;s sent and resolved. Max Influen"}, {"title": "Core Principles", "url": "rules-core-principles.html", "text": "Core Principles\n\nGranted Power. Any mechanic not explicitly described doesn&#x27;t function.\n\n\nSpecific over general. A more specific rule overrides a general one.\n\n    2.1 Example: Inquisitorial Palace \u2265 Established Cunning &gt; general Cunning rule.\n    2.2 When two effects conflict, the one that says can&#x27;t (or doesn&#x27;t) takes precedence over one that says you may or must.\n    2.3 When effects from different sources conflict, the higher source wins: Faction &gt; Monument &gt; Wonder &gt; Standing &gt; Infrastructure = Holding &gt; Action &gt; general rule. Between two effects from the same level, 2.2 decides.\n\nPublic information. All information is public: resources, Domains, Treaties, Armies, Holdings, and Garrisons are known to all players.\n\n\nOnce per turn, same target. A once-per-turn effect can&#x27;t be used on the same target twice in a turn.\n\n\nOne effect per Holding. A Holding has a single effect, active while the Holding is active.\n\n\nDamaged means inactive. A Damaged Holding or Infrastructure has no effect.\n\n\nTimer 0 resolves immediately. Any Timer whose initial value is 0 or less resolves at once.\n\n\nDo as much as possible. Follow as much of an effect as you can;"}, {"title": "Resources", "url": "rules-resources.html", "text": "Resources\n\nGold / Treasury \u2014 your spendable wealth. Pays for Actions, Supply, Upkeep, and Muster recruitment. Running out triggers Insolvency (see Treasury &amp; Upkeep).\nDomain Points \u2014 gain 1 each Rest Phase and spend it to raise a Domain value by 1 (see Domains &amp; Standings).\nInfluence \u2014 the weight you bring to Envoy votes: spend it to Support or Oppose other players&#x27; Envoys (see Actions &amp; Voting).\nRenown \u2014 the score of the table. Gained each Rest Phase and by completing Edicts; it sets the Era.\nPublic Order \u2014 the stability of your realm, raised by Faith and lowered by Doubt. Its band sets ongoing effects (see Public Order).\nFaith \u2014 devotion, generated mostly by Piety Holdings; each Faith raises your Public Order by 1.\nDoubt \u2014 instability; each Doubt lowers your Public Order by 1. Some powerful Holdings cost you Doubt; Cunning and Piety actions give it to others.\n"}, {"title": "The Turn", "url": "rules-the-turn.html", "text": "The Turn\nEach turn runs through five phases in order, then passes the Host and repeats:\n\nEmpire Phase \u2014 Start of the Empire Phase effects, the Season, Timers, Bandit Mechanics, Influence &amp; Envoys, income, Supply and Upkeep, Public Order.\nWorks Phase \u2014 each player performs the Era&#x27;s Works actions (Industry), paying each cost.\nEnvoy Phase \u2014 send all Envoys, a Forum, the Intrigue Phase, vote on every Envoy, the Tally Phase, then resolve them all (Prowess \u2192 Cunning \u2192 Piety \u2192 Industry). In Spring, the Diplomacy Phase replaces it: no Envoys, only Diplomacy offers between players.\nBattle Phase \u2014 Skirmishes, Sieges, and Battles resolve.\nRest Phase \u2014 cleanup, advance the Season, score Renown, spend one Domain Point, pass the Host.\n\nThe Host. Each turn except Spring, one player is the Host. The starting player is always the player directly clockwise from the Host token, including in Spring. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (except in Spring). The Host runs most of the Empire Phase&#x27;s administration: collecting and distributing Trade Income, resolving Bandit Mechanics, and breaking ties (Bandit targeting, and anything not otherwise resolvable). The Host Card carries the "}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "rules-seasons.html", "text": "Seasons\nThe Realm cycles through four Seasons. The current Season&#x27;s effect is applied during the Empire Phase, and the Rest Phase advances the Season by one. Each time the Season changes to Spring, the Year advances by 1.\nSeasonNameEffectWinterFreezingAll Armies gain Speed -5; Siege Timers don&#x27;t count down. Tax income collected.SpringPlantingNo Host, Bandit Actions, Trade Income, or Envoys: the Diplomacy Phase replaces the Envoy Phase, the only time Diplomacy actions happen. Players don&#x27;t gain or spend Influence tokens. Bandit Camps Spawn.SummerCampaigningAll Armies gain Speed +3FallHarvestIncome from Holdings in Hamlets is doubled."}, {"title": "Table Setup", "url": "rules-table-setup.html", "text": "Table Setup\n\nDomain Board: set Renown to 1, set each player&#x27;s Standing in each Domain to 1, set Season to Summer, and set Public Order to 0.\nTactic Decks, Equipment &amp; Retinue Cards, Holding Tiles, Bandit Camps, and the various tokens.\n"}, {"title": "Setup Order", "url": "rules-setup-order.html", "text": "Setup Order\n\nSelect Map \u2014 choose the Hex Map.\nSelect Age \u2014 choose an Age and a starting Year within its range (see Ages). Every player starts Rising in that Age&#x27;s Domain: set that Domain to 3. In the Age of Renown, each player chooses their own Rising Domain. Turn 1 takes place in the starting Year.\nSelect Faction \u2014 pick a Faction Card (optional for new players).\nDetermine Host \u2014 give the Host Card to the most experienced player. If tied, to whoever wants to Host; if still tied, roll off.\nDeploy \u2014 taking turns from the starting player, each player places their capital Town within Range 4 of the board edge or corner. Then each player places their Hamlet exactly Range 2 from their Town. Then each player places their Outlaw Country: its first Territory exactly Range 2 from their Town, and no Outlaw Country Territory within Range 2 of their Hamlet.\nWild Outlaw Country \u2014 the Host scatters the remaining Outlaw Country zones over the unclaimed board (see Outlaw Country).\n\nAges\nAn Age sets the starting Year and which Domain every player starts Rising in.\nAgeStarting RisingStarting YearAge of FractureProwess0\u20131352Age of PlentyIndustry1352\u20131942Age of the TetramorphPiety1942\u20133066Age of D"}, {"title": "Player Setup", "url": "rules-player-setup.html", "text": "Player Setup\n\nEmpire Tableau.\nCollect 10000 Gold, 2 Influence Tokens, and 1 Envoy.\nYou don&#x27;t begin the game with any Armies.\nStarting Holdings \u2014 Select 2 eligible Raw Material Holdings for your capital. Starting Holdings are free and begin the game built.\nStart of Turn 1 check-in \u2014 before the first turn, each player resolves their Start of the Empire Phase effects, including Domain Standing effects (such as a Perform \u2026 Standing action, or Faith from an Each Empire Phase Standing effect). Then the first turn begins at the Works Phase instead of the Empire Phase.\n"}, {"title": "Action Mechanics", "url": "rules-action-mechanics.html", "text": "Action Mechanics\nSending an Envoy\nEnvoys are the currency of actions: to perform an action you send an Envoy during the Envoy Phase. Sending costs 1 Envoy, and you must be able to pay the action&#x27;s cost before you send it. Declare the Domain but not the action \u2014 &quot;I&#x27;d like to send a [Domain] Envoy.&quot; Envoys never target: you choose the action, and its target, only after the Envoy passes, so no one knows exactly what will happen until then.\nResolving an Envoy\nYour Envoy begins with Authority equal to your Standing Rank in its Domain (see Standing Rank), plus any automatic Authority \u00b1X modifiers. (These come from your Holdings, Infrastructure, and Faction, and apply on their own; you never spend Influence for them.)\nThen, clockwise from the starting player and skipping the sender, every other player may respond, with no talking during the vote:\n\nSupport X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to raise the Envoy&#x27;s net Authority.\nOppose X \u2014 spend X of your Influence to lower it.\nAbstain \u2014 spend nothing.\n\nYou spend Influence only when you Support or Oppose; abstaining is free. You can&#x27;t vote on your own Envoy. On a single vote, each player may spend up to their Max Infl"}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "rules-influence.html", "text": "Influence\nEach Empire Phase, gain Influence from the following sources:\nSourceInfluence ChangeNotesEra+1/+2/+3/+4Based on the Current EraTrade Partners+1Per Trade Partner.Alliances+1Per Alliance Member.Infrastructure tier completed+1Per Infrastructure tier fully completed.Fully Mustered Army+1Per active Army of 25 Retinues.Condemned Envoy last turn-1Per Condemned Envoy last turn.At War-3While at War.Monuments &amp; Wonders+1Per active Monument or Wonder.Other sources+XFrom other effects like Holdings.\n"}, {"title": "Diplomacy Actions", "url": "rules-diplomacy-actions.html", "text": "Diplomacy Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSign TreatyNone\u2014Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance. \u2014 When acting on behalf of an Alliance, End Treaty requires all allies to agree.; A player can&#x27;t be in more than one Alliance.Faith +1.NegotiateNone\u2014Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding). \u2014 If a promise goes unfulfilled, the affected player may Declare War on the promiser.; Also used to resolve Demand Tribute and Siege surrenders.Faith +1.End TreatyNone\u2014Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn&#x27;t need to agree.Faith +1.\nDiplomacy actions aren&#x27;t sent as Envoys: they happen only in Spring&#x27;s Diplomacy Phase (see Diplomacy Phase)."}, {"title": "Prowess Actions", "url": "rules-prowess-actions.html", "text": "Prowess Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedMoveNone\u2014Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege. \u2014 Unless the move action was Endorsed, an Army may be the target of only one Move action per turn.; Presence limits where the Army may move (see Rule: Commanding Presence).; While an Army&#x27;s Battle or Siege Timer is active, it can&#x27;t be the target of actions.; When an Army performs the Battle action, it gains Seize the Initiative in that Battle&#x27;s first Skirmish.Perform a Prowess action.Declare WarNoneRising ProwessChoose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you. \u2014 If you are in a Military Alliance, then at the start of your next turn every member Declares War on the target and sends 1 fewer Envoy that turn.Perform a Prowess action.PillageNoneRising Prowe"}, {"title": "Cunning Actions", "url": "rules-cunning-actions.html", "text": "Cunning Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedIntercept Caravan2000 gold\u2014Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income. If they have no Trade Income that turn, instead Extort 100 per their Craft. \u2014 This affects only a single turn&#x27;s trade income; normal income resumes afterward.Extort 2000.Foster Rebellion2000 gold\u2014Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country. \u2014 If that player&#x27;s Outlaw Country has no room, expand it by one Territory and spawn there instead.Extort 2000.Raze2000 gold\u2014Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose another player&#x27;s Settlement, then choose one active Holding or active Infrastructure in it: it becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. If you choose an active Build Timer in it instead, increase that Build Timer by 2. \u2014 A Wonder has Immune Razed and can&#x27;t be targeted.Extort 2000.Destabilize2000 gold\u2014Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose a player. In the next Winter phase, during the Extort step, Extort one settlement&#x27;s tax income. Each"}, {"title": "Piety Actions", "url": "rules-piety-actions.html", "text": "Piety Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedSpread TruthDoubt 1\u2014Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1.Recoup Doubt.Send MissionariesDoubt 1\u2014Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2.Recoup Doubt.TitheDoubt 1\u2014Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0).Recoup Doubt.ConvertDoubt 1Sovereign PietyChoose another player&#x27;s closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be -10 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture). \u2014 If the target&#x27;s Public Order rises to 1 or higher before the timer reaches 0, the Convert fails and the timer is removed.Recoup Doubt.Sacred WarDoubt 1Sovereign PietyDeclare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies. \u2014 While a Sacred War is active, neither player may Declare War on, Sign or End a Treaty with, Negoti"}, {"title": "Industry Actions", "url": "rules-industry-actions.html", "text": "Industry Actions\nActionCostRequiresEffect (if passes)EndorsedImprove2000 gold\u2014Choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time. When it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your Province. \u2014 You must have at least one Infrastructure from the prior tier before building the next tier.; A Wonder is built in your capital; you build one Wonder at a time.Recoup 2000.Repair0 gold\u2014Choose a Damaged Holding or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Repair Timer 1. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Holding tile from your Empire Tableau.Recoup 0.Build2000 gold\u2014Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Holding with one complete line of its Mastery Chain under your control (and meet its other requirements) and set a Build Timer equal to its build time (usually 1). When it completes, place the Holding in an available Ward slot; its effect activates immediately. \u2014 You may have only 1 Monument Holdings per settlement.; Build Timer by Standing: Untested 0, Rising 1, Established 2, Sovereign 3.Recoup 2000.Settle2000 goldRising IndustryCha"}, {"title": "Domains & Standings", "url": "rules-domains-standings.html", "text": "Domains &amp; Standings\nDomain Standings\nDomains are the identity of your character in Renown. As you gain Renown each turn, you gain a Domain Point, which you may spend in any of the four Domains. Each Domain Point raises your Domain value by 1 in that Domain. When your Domain value reaches 3, you become Rising in that Domain \u2014 you may spend one extra Influence on another player&#x27;s Envoy of that Domain, and your Envoys gain Authority +1. This continues at a Domain value of 6 (Established) and again at 10 (Sovereign).\nEach Standing you gain in a Domain makes you harder to oppose there and lets you oppose others more easily with your Influence. You also gain a unique effect at each Standing that makes it easier to achieve that Domain&#x27;s objectives. A Standing effect that lets you perform an action (Perform \u2026) is one-time: you use it at the Start of the next Empire Phase after you reach that Standing (a Standing you start the game with: the Start of Turn 1 check-in). Every other Standing effect applies for as long as you hold that Standing; its Each Empire Phase effects resolve at the Start of the Empire Phase.\nStanding Rank\nEach Standing has a Standing Rank: Untested 1, Risi"}, {"title": "Diplomacy & Treaties", "url": "rules-diplomacy-treaties.html", "text": "Diplomacy &amp; Treaties\nTreaties &amp; Alliances\nTreatySigned ViaEraEffectPeace TreatySign TreatyAnyEnds war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5.Trade AgreementSign TreatyAnyBegin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect for each player.Non-Aggression PactSign TreatyAnyNeither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5.Military AllianceSign TreatyEminenceMutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy).Defensive AllianceSign TreatyZenithMutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker.\nAlliance Rules:\nNew alliance members are added by unanimous agreement.A player cannot be in more than one alliance at a time.An alliance may remove a member via End Treaty if all others agree.\nVassalization\nTo vassalize a player:\n\nControl that player&#x27;s capital Settlement while the player has no other Settlements or Armies under their Control.\n\n\nAt the end of the Rest Phase, return every Settlement you Control that was chartered by that player to that player. You become their Suzerain, and"}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "rules-settlements.html", "text": "Settlements\nSettlements are the primary vehicle of your Empire. They come in tiers: Village, Town, City, and a capital Metropolis. Each tier provides tax income each Winter, Settlement Wards that a Holding can fill, and a per-turn Muster limit of Retinues. The values per tier are below:\nSettlementTaxMusterWardsReachBuildNotesHamlet00311Natural holdings only; Placed at start of game Range 2 from capital.Village20005122Town400010244City600025366Metropolis800050488Capital only, requires Sovereign Industry (Titan of Industry)\nSettlement Wards\nA Settlement Ward is a slot that holds one Holding. Each Ward occupies a Territory within Range 1 of its Settlement; while you have a Keep, your Wards have Presence. A Settlement has one Ward per tier: a Village has 1, a Town 2, a City 3 and a Metropolis 4. A Hamlet has 3 Wards.\nChartering Settlements\nWhen you Settle a new Village, place it on Grassland (a Hill counts) that is in your Province or within the Presence of one of your Armies, and at least Range 2 from any Outlaw Country.\nSettlement Reach\nSettlements have a Reach value set by their tier, from 2 up to 8. Reach X determines which Territory you Control in your Province: at Reach 1 you Con"}, {"title": "Infrastructure", "url": "rules-infrastructure.html", "text": "Infrastructure\nInfrastructure is the foundation of your Settlements. Each active Infrastructure provides an effect that applies to your entire empire and all its Settlements.\nExample: Wooden Walls defend every one of your Settlements, and a Cathedral gives you Faith +1 each turn, however many Settlements you have.\nInfrastructure comes in 5 ascending tiers. Primitive Infrastructure builds the basic blocks of your empire. Developed Infrastructure expands and replaces some Primitive Infrastructure. Sophisticated Infrastructure allows more powerful effects and helps unlock unique Monument Holdings. Prodigious Infrastructure comes next, and Wondrous Infrastructure \u2014 the world Wonders \u2014 is the highest tier.\nTo build any Infrastructure, you need at least one active Infrastructure of the tier below it \u2014 so Developed needs one Primitive, Sophisticated needs one Developed (and therefore one Primitive), and so on up to Wondrous. One Tier Primitive means any one Primitive Infrastructure. Some Infrastructure also names its own requirement on top of this: a Library needs a Town Hall, and a Magistrate&#x27;s Hall needs a Library.\nWonders are the Wondrous tier, with Realm Scope: each is built once"}, {"title": "Territory & Terrain", "url": "rules-territory-terrain.html", "text": "Territory &amp; Terrain\nTerritory is the smallest unit of land. To move from one Territory to another, you move Range 1. To be within a Territory is Range 0; adjacent is Range 1; next to is Range 2.\nSpeed X \u2014 An Army&#x27;s movement in Territories per Move action. Base Speed is 5.\nTerritories carry modifiers by hex type (grassland, forest, barrens, wetlands, water, mountain), and are Uncontrolled, Contested, or Controlled. Territory begins Uncontrolled. By chartering Settlements you Control Territories: each Settlement&#x27;s Reach X adds every Territory within that Range to your Province. If another player&#x27;s Settlement Reach reaches any Territory you Control, that Territory is Contested.\nTo border another player, your Reach must be within or adjacent to their Territory.\nTerrainMap EffectRaw MaterialsBattle EffectGrasslandWhere Settlements can be chartered (a Hill counts).Common LandHill: If you Battle while your army is on a Hill, gain +1 Initiative every Skirmish. A Hill counts as Open Field: Ranged Weapons gain +1 to Strike.  Open Field: Ranged Weapons gain +1 to Strike.WetlandsSpeed \u22121 per Territory moved throughPeat Bog, ForestryMire: Gain Unwieldy and Immune Steady; \u22121 t"}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "rules-public-order.html", "text": "Public Order\nFaith and Doubt adjust your Public Order the moment they&#x27;re generated \u2014 each Faith raises it by 1, each Doubt lowers it by 1, applied immediately. Public Order is capped between \u221210 and 10. Bands stack: every band between Neutral and your current value is active, so each step further from Neutral adds its effect to the ones before it. A band&#x27;s X is its value in the current Era (the Era columns of the table).\nFirst Doubt of the turn. Some effects (e.g. Reliquary, Episcopal Court) reduce the first Doubt (or first two) you gain each turn, from any source \u2014 each instance of Doubt uses up one reduction. Because Doubt applies immediately, this is whichever Doubt lands first in the turn \u2014 usually your innate modifiers in the Empire Phase, but it can be an opponent&#x27;s action if that resolves first. Track whether you&#x27;ve taken Doubt yet this turn; the marker resets at the Start of each Empire Phase, before innate modifiers apply.\nYour innate Faith and Doubt \u2014 from Holdings, Infrastructure, and the modifiers below \u2014 are checked once each turn during the Empire Phase. Add them all up (after any first-Doubt reductions), apply the net change, then cap the result: "}, {"title": "Treasury & Upkeep", "url": "rules-treasury-upkeep.html", "text": "Treasury &amp; Upkeep\nYour Treasury is the gold you Control. Each Empire Phase you gain your Revenue (tax, trade, and Holding income) and pay your Supply (Armies) and Upkeep (Holdings and Infrastructure); the net lands in your Treasury. Costs you pay during the turn come out of the same Treasury.\nHolding Upkeep and Build Timer follow the Holding&#x27;s Standing requirement \u2014 by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 0), Rising 200 (Build Timer 1), Established 300 (Build Timer 2), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 3); Natural 0. Holdings and Infrastructure only pay Upkeep while active: none while being built, Damaged, under repair, or Shuttered.\nSupply is what your Armies cost: the sum of each Army&#x27;s cost (by Retinue type), minus every Supply \u2212X (never below 0). Upkeep \u2212X lowers Holding and Infrastructure Upkeep the same way. Army costs by Retinue type: Levy 1000, Man-at-Arms 2000, Sergeant 3000, Knight Templar 3000.\nTracking tip: keep three small piles \u2014 Treasury, Revenue, and costs (Supply and Upkeep). When you build or muster something with income or a cost, add it to the matching pile; when it&#x27;s Damaged or an Army is disbanded, subtract it. Each turn it&#x27;s just Treasury + Re"}, {"title": "Trade & Income", "url": "rules-trade-income.html", "text": "Trade &amp; Income\nWho Can Trade\nWho can trade: a player needs a signed Trade Agreement and either active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect (e.g. Harbor).\nCraft X: Craft Holdings count toward how much income your Trade Agreements generate \u2014 any effect that grants Craft +X.\nTrade income: for each active Trade Agreement, both players gain gold equal to 100 \u00d7 the Host&#x27;s Craft X.\nWhen income flows:\n\nWhen you sign a Trade Agreement: the player who did not perform the Sign Treaty action gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host. Afterwards, both get trade income each turn either of them is Host.\nWhen you end a Trade Agreement: the player who ended it gets trade income the next time they&#x27;re Host, then trading ceases.\n\nRuleValueIncome per Craft100RequirementsA signed Trade Agreement, and each player has active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect (e.g. Harbor, Shipyard)No-trade SeasonSpring\nIncome Types\n\nTaxes: each Winter, in the Income &amp; Upkeep step of the Empire Phase, gain tax income from each of your Settlements by tier, after modifiers.\nTrade: see above.\nHoldings: gain Holding income in the Income &amp; Upkeep step of the Empire Phase.\n\nGlossary \u00b7 Economy &amp; Publi"}, {"title": "Armies", "url": "rules-armies.html", "text": "Armies\nArmies Overview\nArmies are collections of Retinues on the Realm, and are the target of Move actions. An Army holds up to 25 Retinues and up to a single piece of equipment of each type (armor, weapon, shield, and Retinue). Armies cost Supply each Empire Phase (see Treasury &amp; Upkeep).\nWhile an Army is engaged in a Battle or Lay Siege action started by another player&#x27;s Army, neither Army can be the target of any actions until that Battle or Lay Siege resolves.\nGarrisons\nA Garrison is an Army that exists within each of your Settlements while you have the Garrison Infrastructure, sized by that Settlement&#x27;s Garrison value (Village 10, Town 15, City 25, Metropolis 50 Retinues). Garrisons can&#x27;t perform actions or be targeted by actions, and may Sally Forth while their Settlement is under Siege. Garrisons have cost and Supply 0 and don&#x27;t count toward your Army limit. All Garrisons within an Empire share the same Retinue type and equipment, and gain the benefits of all unlocked keywords that apply to your Armies.\nMustering\nArmies are raised and reinforced with the Muster action (see Prowess Actions).\nDuring the Income &amp; Upkeep step, while an Army is within "}, {"title": "Battle Phase", "url": "rules-battle-phase.html", "text": "Battle Phase\nA Battle is fought as a series of Skirmishes, run through the steps below until one side is wiped out, Routs, or successfully Falls Back. Full keyword detail is in the glossary tables at the end of this section.\nBeginning a Battle\n\nDeclare Army \u2014 declare which Army will Skirmish (if more than one is adjacent to either Army in the Battle).\n\n\nSeize the Initiative \u2014 the player who performed the Battle action usually gains Seize the Initiative, but Terrain and the Ministry of Military Strategy can change that. That player gains Initiative +1 in the first Skirmish.\n\nThe Skirmish Steps\n\nForm the line. Each side places up to 10 Retinues in its front line \u2014 one Strike die each \u2014 and may keep up to 5 in reserve to replace losses as they fall. An Army of 25 keeps the remainder in camp; between Skirmishes, camp and reserves refill the front line and reserve to their maximums.\n\n\nChoose Tactics and equipment. Both players secretly pick one Tactic and, if they have a choice, the equipment they&#x27;ll use this Skirmish (an Army carrying both a Ranged and a Melee weapon picks one; a Bastard Sword picks its 1H or 2H profile; an Army with Florentine may Dual Wield its 1H Melee Weapon i"}, {"title": "Siege Warfare", "url": "rules-siege-warfare.html", "text": "Siege Warfare\n\nWhen you Lay Siege during the Envoy Phase, track the relevant Siege Timer(s).\nWhen a Siege Timer reaches 0, resolve the Siege before the Rest Phase: negotiate, then Battle if needed, then Capture or Sack.\n\nSiege Timer\nA Siege Timer is the sum of the besieged Settlement&#x27;s defenses minus the attacker&#x27;s Siege effects, to a minimum of 1 (no maximum). Every source below stacks \u2014 Wooden Walls and Stone Walls both count.\nSourceTimerNoteSettlement Size+0 to +4Hamlet 0, Village 1, Town 2, City 3, Metropolis 4Citadel+4Holding; only in its own SettlementStanding Army+1Army within Range 0 of the SettlementOffice of Works+2HoldingWooden Walls+1InfrastructureStone Walls+1InfrastructureKeep+1InfrastructureThe Iron Faith+3Faction; While your Public Order is 4 or higherAttacker effects\u2212 variesArtillery Park \u22122, Colossus \u22122, Siege Camp \u22121, Siege Works \u22121\nBeginning a Siege\n\nEnd a Move action with your Army adjacent to another player&#x27;s Settlement you&#x27;re At War with.\n\n\nYour Army must stay there for the Siege Timer and can&#x27;t take other actions.\n\n\nIf you&#x27;re attacked while sieging and you Fall Back, the Siege is broken and the Siege Timer is removed from play.\n"}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "rules-bandits.html", "text": "Bandits\nOutlaw Country\nOutlaw Country is zones of Territory no player can Control, where Bandit Camps spawn. Setup places zones in two ways; after Setup, every zone works the same.\n\nYour zone (Deploy): demarcate 3 Territories in your starting region, each within Range 1 of at least one other Outlaw Country Territory and at least Range 2 from any Settlement \u2014 the first exactly Range 2 from your Town, and none within Range 2 of your Hamlet. If that&#x27;s not possible, place them Range 2 from your capital Settlement.\nWild zones (last Setup step): the Host scatters more zones over the unclaimed board \u2014 the number of players \u00f7 0, rounded down, + 0. Each is 3 connected Territories, none on mountain or water Territory, at least Range 3 from every player&#x27;s Province and at least Range 5 from every other Outlaw Country zone. Each Province starts the game with exactly one Outlaw Country zone.\n\nA zone is your Outlaw Country while any of its Territories is within your Province. A zone in no player&#x27;s Province belongs to no one: its camps spawn and grow, but take no action until they&#x27;re within a player&#x27;s Province; a camp that grows into a Bandit Army Marches like any other.\nS"}, {"title": "Holdings", "url": "rules-holdings.html", "text": "Holdings\nHoldings are listed by the Standing they require, Domain by Domain; Monuments are marked (Monument) and Natural Holdings (Natural). A Holding that requires two Standings appears under both.\nNo RequirementHoldingInfrastructure ReqMastery ChainEffectAlchemy\u2014Peat BogGold +500; Craft +2Animal Husbandry (Natural)\u2014HamletSupply \u2212500; Unlocks Crude armor &amp; shieldApiary (Natural)\u2014\u2014Gold +500; Craft +1Apothecary\u2014AlchemyGold +500; Gain Recover 8, or improve Recover by +1Bakery (Natural)\u2014HamletGold +500; Faith +1Butchery (Natural)\u2014Salt Works, Animal HusbandryCraft +3; Supply \u2212500Caravanery (Natural)\u2014Courier NetworkAuthority \u22122 on Intercept Caravan actions targeting you; Speed \u22122 to non-allied Armies in your ProvinceCarpentry\u2014ForestryGold +500; Craft +1; Build Timer \u22121Chandlery\u2014ApiaryCraft +1; Authority \u22121 on Cunning actions targeting youCharcoal Burner (Natural)\u2014ButcheryGold +1000Common Land (Natural)\u2014HamletGold +1000; Doubt +1Courier Network (Natural)\u2014InnIn the Intrigue Phase: Authority \u22121 on one EnvoyCourtyardTown Square\u2014Craft +1; Faith +1Fishmongery (Natural)\u2014\u2014Gold +500; Craft +2Forestry (Natural)\u2014\u2014Gold +500; Craft +1Furnace (Natural)\u2014\u2014Gold +500; Unlocks Cast WeaponsHerb Garden "}, {"title": "Melee Weapons", "url": "rules-melee-weapons.html", "text": "Melee Weapons\nWeaponTierAPInitKeywordsFarm ToolCrude0+0AwkwardCudgelCrude\u22121\u221212H, Unwieldy, AwkwardPitchforkCrude0+12H, Unwieldy, AwkwardDaggersCast0+02H, Deadly, AwkwardShort SwordCast0+0SteadySpearCast\u22121+1UnwieldyArming SwordWrought\u22121+0SteadyPikeWrought\u22122+12H, Steady, Unwieldy, Deadly, AwkwardFlailWrought\u22121+0Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Cleave, AwkwardHalberdWrought\u22122+02H, SteadyBattle AxeWrought\u22123\u221212H, Unstoppable, Cleave, Negate ShieldedCavalry SpearWrought\u22122+1Steady, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, AwkwardMorningstarForged\u22124\u22121Cleave, Destroy ShieldBastard SwordForged\u22122+0Steady2HBastardForged\u22122+02H, Unstoppable, CleaveWar HammerForged\u221210\u221212H, Steady, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Destroy ShieldLanceForged\u22124+1Steady, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Awkward, Destroy ShieldEstocTempered\u22123+0Steady, Deadly, UnstoppablePoleaxeTempered\u22125+02H, Steady, Cleave, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded"}, {"title": "Ranged Weapons", "url": "rules-ranged-weapons.html", "text": "Ranged Weapons\nRanged WeaponTierAPInitKeywordsHunting BowCrude0+22H, Unstoppable, AwkwardLongbowCast\u22121+22H, Unstoppable, Deadly, AwkwardThrowing AxeWrought\u22122+1Steady, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Destroy Shield, One-Shot, AwkwardCrossbowForged\u22124+12H, Unwieldy, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, AwkwardThrowing SpearTempered\u22125+1Steady, Deadly, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Destroy Shield, One-Shot, AwkwardArquebusGunpowder\u22126+22H, Unwieldy, Unstoppable, Negate Shielded, Awkward"}, {"title": "Shields", "url": "rules-shields.html", "text": "Shields\nShieldTierSave BonusInitKeywordsNone\u2014+0+0\u2014Buckler ShieldCrude+1+0\u2014Targe ShieldCast+1+0Unwieldy, ShieldedKite ShieldWrought+1+0Steady, ShieldedTower ShieldForged+2+0Unwieldy, ShieldedHeater ShieldTempered+2+0Shielded, Immune Destroy Shield"}, {"title": "Armor", "url": "rules-armor.html", "text": "Armor\nArmorTierSaveKeywordsClothNone10+\u2014GambesonCrude8+\u2014LeatherCast7+\u2014ChainmailWrought6+\u2014Full PlateForged5+\u2014Gothic PlateTempered4+\u2014\nGlossary \u00b7 Equipment TiersTermDefinitionCrudeCrude equipment tier. Weapons: Farm Tools, Cudgel, Pitchfork; Ranged: Hunting Bow; Armor: Gambeson; Shield: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry (armor &amp; shield).CastCast equipment tier. Weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spears; Ranged: Longbow; Armor: Leather; Shield: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Furnace (weapons), Tannery (armor &amp; shield).WroughtWrought equipment tier. Weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear; Ranged: Javelin; Armor: Chainmail; Shield: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Blacksmith (weapons), Armory (armor &amp; shield).ForgedForged equipment tier. Weapons: Morningstar, Bastard Sword, 2HBastard, War Hammer, Lance; Ranged: Crossbow; Armor: Full Plate; Shield: Tower Shield. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry (armor &amp; shield), Forge (all).TemperedTempered equipment tier. Weapons: Estoc, Poleaxe; Ranged: Pilum; Armor: Gothic Plate; Shield: Heater Shield. Unlocked by: Court Armoury (armor &amp; shield), Advanced Blast Furnace (weapons).GunpowderGunpowder equipment: "}, {"title": "Factions", "url": "rules-factions.html", "text": "Factions\nFactionFeelDifficultyStrengthMechanicThe Battering RamOffensive, ArrogantLowMediumYou begin the game with a Siege Works (no Ward, Natural).The Boundless SteppeFastLowMediumYou begin the game with a Stable (no Ward, Natural).The Bandit KingScrappyHighHighYou begin the game with a Smuggler&#x27;s Nook (no Ward, Natural). At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may control one Bandit Camp outside your Territory. When a Bandit Camp is spawned, you may place it in your Outlaw Country instead. You cannot Build Holdings which require Piety or Prowess Standing.The Crimson TidePirate LifeLowMediumOther players can&#x27;t perform Intercept Caravan on you. You begin the game with a Shipyard (no Ward, Natural).The Entwined CrownDiplomatic, InescapableLowMediumOnce per game, you may join an Alliance without unanimous consent, or form one with a player who isn&#x27;t in an Alliance. While in that Alliance, each member gains Faith +1 and Influence +1 each Empire Phase.The Eternal CourtPatient &amp; ReservedLowMediumYour unspent Influence isn&#x27;t discarded in the Rest Phase. While the Era is Zenith, your Max Influence is 5 on every Envoy.The Final WordCold SteelLowMediumIgnore the innate"}, {"title": "Index", "url": "rules-index.html", "text": "Index\n"}, {"title": "Carpentry", "url": "type-arms.html#carpentry", "text": "Carpentry Arms Gold +500; Craft +1; Build Timer -1 "}, {"title": "Fletchery", "url": "type-arms.html#fletchery", "text": "Fletchery Arms Supply -500; Unlocks Ranged Weapons "}, {"title": "Tannery", "url": "type-arms.html#tannery", "text": "Tannery Arms Craft +1; Supply -500; Unlocks Cast armor & shield "}, {"title": "Joinery", "url": "type-arms.html#joinery", "text": "Joinery Arms Supply -500; Unlocks Shields "}, {"title": "Blacksmith", "url": "type-arms.html#blacksmith", "text": "Blacksmith Arms Craft +2; Supply -500; Unlocks Wrought Weapons "}, {"title": "Armory", "url": "type-arms.html#armory", "text": "Armory Arms Craft +2; Supply -500; Unlocks Wrought armor & shield "}, {"title": "Master Workshop", "url": "type-arms.html#master-workshop", "text": "Master Workshop Arms Craft +2; Supply -500; Add Serrated to Weapons "}, {"title": "Gilded Foundry", "url": "type-arms.html#gilded-foundry", "text": "Gilded Foundry Arms Supply -1000; Unlocks Forged armor & shield "}, {"title": "Stable", "url": "type-arms.html#stable", "text": "Stable Arms Speed +1; Unlocks Cavalry Spear (Still requires Tier Unlock) "}, {"title": "Forge", "url": "type-arms.html#forge", "text": "Forge Arms Craft +2; Unlocks Forged Tier Weapons "}, {"title": "Skirmish Field", "url": "type-arms.html#skirmish-field", "text": "Skirmish Field Arms Armies may be equipped with a Ranged and a Melee Weapon simultaneously; Unlocks Longbow regardless of Unlock Tier "}, {"title": "List Yard", "url": "type-arms.html#list-yard", "text": "List Yard Arms Gain Immune Awkward; gain Florentine "}, {"title": "Butchery", "url": "type-logistics.html#butchery", "text": "Butchery Logistics Craft +3; Supply -500 "}, {"title": "Smokehouse", "url": "type-logistics.html#smokehouse", "text": "Smokehouse Logistics Craft +2; Supply -1000 "}, {"title": "Caravanery", "url": "type-logistics.html#caravanery", "text": "Caravanery Logistics Authority -2 on Intercept Caravan actions targeting you; Speed -2 to non-allied Armies in your Province "}, {"title": "Coliseum", "url": "type-logistics.html#coliseum", "text": "Coliseum Logistics Faith +1 while at War; Unlocks Man-at-Arms for Muster "}, {"title": "Conditioning Field", "url": "type-logistics.html#conditioning-field", "text": "Conditioning Field Logistics Faith +1 while not at War; Armies gain Nimble "}, {"title": "Grand Tournament", "url": "type-logistics.html#grand-tournament", "text": "Grand Tournament Logistics Reach +1; Armies gain Riposte & Improve Parry by +1 "}, {"title": "Charcoal Burner", "url": "type-logistics.html#charcoal-burner", "text": "Charcoal Burner Logistics Gold +1000 "}, {"title": "Levy Hall", "url": "type-logistics.html#levy-hall", "text": "Levy Hall Logistics Speed +1; Supply -2000 while an Army is within Range 0 of a Settlement you Control "}, {"title": "Siege Camp", "url": "type-logistics.html#siege-camp", "text": "Siege Camp Logistics Siege Timer -1; Armies gain Immune Strained during Lay Siege "}, {"title": "Siege Works", "url": "type-logistics.html#siege-works", "text": "Siege Works Logistics Siege Timer -1; Siege Timers count down in Winter "}, {"title": "Battery Park", "url": "type-logistics.html#battery-park", "text": "Battery Park Logistics Your Siege Timers count down twice each turn instead of once "}, {"title": "War College", "url": "type-logistics.html#war-college", "text": "War College Logistics Influence +2 while At War; Unlocks Sergeants for Muster "}, {"title": "Masonry", "url": "type-works.html#masonry", "text": "Masonry Works Build Timer -1; No Upkeep on Primitive Infrastructure "}, {"title": "Workyard", "url": "type-works.html#workyard", "text": "Workyard Works Gold +1000; Doubt +1 "}, {"title": "Storehouse", "url": "type-works.html#storehouse", "text": "Storehouse Works Upkeep -2000; Doubt +1; Build Timer -1 "}, {"title": "Census Hall", "url": "type-works.html#census-hall", "text": "Census Hall Works Gold +1000; Craft +3; Doubt +1 "}, {"title": "Supply Depot", "url": "type-works.html#supply-depot", "text": "Supply Depot Works Upkeep -500; Supply -500; Armies and Garrisons within your Settlements gain Immune Strained "}, {"title": "Trade Guild", "url": "type-works.html#trade-guild", "text": "Trade Guild Works Repair Timer -1; No Upkeep on Developed Infrastructure "}, {"title": "College of Engineering", "url": "type-works.html#college-of-engineering", "text": "College of Engineering Works Build Timer -1; No Upkeep on Sophisticated Infrastructure "}, {"title": "Masons' Guild", "url": "type-works.html#masons-guild", "text": "Masons' Guild Works Build Timer -1; No Upkeep on Prodigious Infrastructure "}, {"title": "Burgages", "url": "type-works.html#burgages", "text": "Burgages Works Faith +1; Upkeep -500 "}, {"title": "Citadel", "url": "type-works.html#citadel", "text": "Citadel Works Siege Timer +4; May Muster an Army in a Settlement under Siege and its Muster Timers count down "}, {"title": "Castle Hall", "url": "type-works.html#castle-hall", "text": "Castle Hall Works Doubt +1; Upkeep -1000; Tax Income is Doubled; Your Settlements gain Reach +2 "}, {"title": "Alchemy", "url": "type-commerce.html#alchemy", "text": "Alchemy Commerce Gold +500; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Finery", "url": "type-commerce.html#finery", "text": "Finery Commerce Craft +3; Weapons gain -1AP "}, {"title": "Jewelry Foundry", "url": "type-commerce.html#jewelry-foundry", "text": "Jewelry Foundry Commerce Gold +2000; Craft +5; In the Envoy Phase, a player may target you with a Cunning Envoy. If they do, that Envoy gains Authority +1. If it Passes or is Endorsed, the action must target you "}, {"title": "Market Square", "url": "type-commerce.html#market-square", "text": "Market Square Commerce Gold +500; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Spice Merchant", "url": "type-commerce.html#spice-merchant", "text": "Spice Merchant Commerce Gold +1000; Craft +4; In the Envoy Phase, a player may target you with a Cunning Envoy. If they do, that Envoy gains Authority +1. If it Passes or is Endorsed, the action must target you "}, {"title": "Harbor", "url": "type-commerce.html#harbor", "text": "Harbor Commerce Can Trade; Craft +2; Extort 500 per player without Harbor "}, {"title": "Merchant Quarter", "url": "type-commerce.html#merchant-quarter", "text": "Merchant Quarter Commerce Craft +5; Trade Partners gain Craft +3 "}, {"title": "Money Lending", "url": "type-commerce.html#money-lending", "text": "Money Lending Commerce Once per Empire Phase, you may loan money to another player at 100 per 1000/turn interest (minimum 100); on Default: Perform Demand Tribute; Extort 1000 "}, {"title": "Esteemed Bank", "url": "type-commerce.html#esteemed-bank", "text": "Esteemed Bank Commerce Each Empire Phase, Gain 1000 per 10000 in Treasury "}, {"title": "Shipyard", "url": "type-commerce.html#shipyard", "text": "Shipyard Commerce Upkeep -500; Craft +4; Water Territory treated as Grassland for movement "}, {"title": "Courtyard", "url": "type-commerce.html#courtyard", "text": "Courtyard Commerce Craft +1; Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Artisan Workshop", "url": "type-commerce.html#artisan-workshop", "text": "Artisan Workshop Commerce Gold +1000; Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Court Artists", "url": "type-commerce.html#court-artists", "text": "Court Artists Commerce Extort 500 twice; Targets of Extort from Court Artist gain Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Emporium", "url": "type-commerce.html#emporium", "text": "Emporium Commerce Gold +1000; Trade Partners gain Craft +3 "}, {"title": "Chandlery", "url": "type-devotion.html#chandlery", "text": "Chandlery Devotion Craft +1; Authority -1 on Cunning actions targeting you "}, {"title": "Interrogation Chambers", "url": "type-devotion.html#interrogation-chambers", "text": "Interrogation Chambers Devotion Extort 500; Doubt from actions targeting you is reduced by 1 (minimum 0) "}, {"title": "Priory", "url": "type-devotion.html#priory", "text": "Priory Devotion Faith +1; If your Piety Envoy would be Condemned, it Fails instead "}, {"title": "Abbey", "url": "type-devotion.html#abbey", "text": "Abbey Devotion Upkeep -500; Authority -2 on Piety actions targeting you "}, {"title": "Reliquary", "url": "type-devotion.html#reliquary", "text": "Reliquary Devotion Faith +1; First two Doubt each turn reduced by 1 "}, {"title": "Monastery", "url": "type-devotion.html#monastery", "text": "Monastery Devotion Influence +2; Your Settlements gain Reach +2 "}, {"title": "Execution Dock", "url": "type-devotion.html#execution-dock", "text": "Execution Dock Devotion Authority -2 on Foster Rebellion actions targeting you; Players whose actions targeting you would cause Doubt (before modifiers) gain Doubt +1 "}, {"title": "Hospitaller", "url": "type-devotion.html#hospitaller", "text": "Hospitaller Devotion Recover improved by +1; Enduring: Successful Recovered rolls do not count towards the panic check threshold "}, {"title": "Episcopal Court", "url": "type-devotion.html#episcopal-court", "text": "Episcopal Court Devotion Faith +1; Reduce the first instance of Doubt each turn by 1, min 0 "}, {"title": "Apothecary", "url": "type-devotion.html#apothecary", "text": "Apothecary Devotion Gold +500; Gain Recover 8, or improve Recover by +1 "}, {"title": "Infirmary", "url": "type-devotion.html#infirmary", "text": "Infirmary Devotion Gold +500; Improve Recover by +1 "}, {"title": "Pilgrimage Site", "url": "type-devotion.html#pilgrimage-site", "text": "Pilgrimage Site Devotion Faith +1; Extort 500 from each other player without a Pilgrimage Site; each other player without a Pilgrimage Site gains Doubt +1 "}, {"title": "Unforgotten Shrine", "url": "type-devotion.html#unforgotten-shrine", "text": "Unforgotten Shrine Devotion When your Piety actions give their target Faith, it gains Faith +1 more; when they give Doubt, it gains Doubt +1 more "}, {"title": "Inn", "url": "type-court.html#inn", "text": "Inn Court Influence +1; Faith +1 per Trade Partner with Craft 3+, and those Trade Partners gain Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Jester's Court", "url": "type-court.html#jester-s-court", "text": "Jester's Court Court First and second Oppose on an Envoy of yours each Envoy Phase: reduce by 1 "}, {"title": "Bell Tower", "url": "type-court.html#bell-tower", "text": "Bell Tower Court Influence +1; Upkeep -500 "}, {"title": "Embassy", "url": "type-court.html#embassy", "text": "Embassy Court Once per Diplomacy Phase, you may cause a Diplomacy action to fail; Other non-vassal players gain Faith +1 per Signed Treaty with you besides Peace "}, {"title": "Academy", "url": "type-court.html#academy", "text": "Academy Court Influence +2 "}, {"title": "University", "url": "type-court.html#university", "text": "University Court Influence +1 per Domain you are Rising; Max Influence +1 on every Envoy "}, {"title": "Collegium Archives", "url": "type-court.html#collegium-archives", "text": "Collegium Archives Court Influence +1 per Established Standing; Authority +1 on every Envoy "}, {"title": "Courier Network", "url": "type-court.html#courier-network", "text": "Courier Network Court In the Intrigue Phase: Authority -1 on one Envoy "}, {"title": "Toll House", "url": "type-secrecy.html#toll-house", "text": "Toll House Secrecy Extort 2000 when non-allied Army ends a Move action within your Province "}, {"title": "Secret Cellar", "url": "type-secrecy.html#secret-cellar", "text": "Secret Cellar Secrecy Passed Cunning envoys Recoup 500 Gold; Endorsed Cunning envoys Recoup 1000 Gold "}, {"title": "Smuggler's Nook", "url": "type-secrecy.html#smuggler-s-nook", "text": "Smuggler's Nook Secrecy Whenever a Bandit Camp within your Province Extorts, you Extort the Bandit Camp for half the amount "}, {"title": "Syndicate Hub", "url": "type-secrecy.html#syndicate-hub", "text": "Syndicate Hub Secrecy Both Bandit Camps & you have Authority +1 on Personal Cunning Envoys; Endorsed Foster Rebellion instead places Bandit Armies with 25 retinues "}, {"title": "Black Market", "url": "type-secrecy.html#black-market", "text": "Black Market Secrecy When another player Extorts gold from any source: Extort 100 per 500 from that player at the end of that resolution; When another player Recoups gold from any source: Extort 100 per 500 from that player at the end of that resolution "}, {"title": "Dark Scriptorium", "url": "type-secrecy.html#dark-scriptorium", "text": "Dark Scriptorium Secrecy Extort 300 anytime a player Opposes an Envoy of yours "}, {"title": "Forgery Workshop", "url": "type-secrecy.html#forgery-workshop", "text": "Forgery Workshop Secrecy At the end of the Tally Phase, if a Cunning Envoy you sent Failed, you may send another Cunning Envoy "}, {"title": "Toxicarium", "url": "type-secrecy.html#toxicarium", "text": "Toxicarium Secrecy Weapons gain Poison; Endorsed Cunning envoys give an additional Doubt +1 to Target "}, {"title": "Charnel House", "url": "type-secrecy.html#charnel-house", "text": "Charnel House Secrecy Indecisive, Aimless, & Recession effects are doubled for all players "}, {"title": "Plague Pit", "url": "type-secrecy.html#plague-pit", "text": "Plague Pit Secrecy No longer affected by all Public Order effects (positive or negative); Convert actions can't target you "}, {"title": "Beacon Towers", "url": "type-secrecy.html#beacon-towers", "text": "Beacon Towers Secrecy At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may select an Army within your Province and move it up to its modified Speed; Whenever a non-allied Army ends a Move action within your Province, you may immediately perform a Move action "}, {"title": "Forgotten Catacombs", "url": "type-secrecy.html#forgotten-catacombs", "text": "Forgotten Catacombs Secrecy Cunning actions targeting you can't be Endorsed "}, {"title": "Cipher Chamber", "url": "type-secrecy.html#cipher-chamber", "text": "Cipher Chamber Secrecy At the Start of the Empire Phase, choose one: select an army you did not select last turn; that army gains Blocked; or select any active Timer you did not select last turn; increase it by 2 "}, {"title": "Herb Garden", "url": "type-husbandry.html#herb-garden", "text": "Herb Garden Husbandry Gold +500; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Animal Husbandry", "url": "type-husbandry.html#animal-husbandry", "text": "Animal Husbandry Husbandry Supply -500; Unlocks Crude armor & shield "}, {"title": "Saddlery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#saddlery", "text": "Saddlery Husbandry Gold +500; Speed +1; Unlocks Lance (Still requires Tier Unlock) "}, {"title": "Avenery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#avenery", "text": "Avenery Husbandry Gold +1000; Speed +1 "}, {"title": "Farriery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#farriery", "text": "Farriery Husbandry Gold +1000; Speed +1; Unlocks Cavalry Spears regardless of Tier Unlock "}, {"title": "Vineyard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#vineyard", "text": "Vineyard Husbandry Gold +1000 in Fall "}, {"title": "Orchard", "url": "type-husbandry.html#orchard", "text": "Orchard Husbandry Gold +500; Gold +500 in Fall "}, {"title": "Bakery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#bakery", "text": "Bakery Husbandry Gold +500; Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Meadery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#meadery", "text": "Meadery Husbandry Faith +1; Speed +5 in Winter "}, {"title": "Winery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#winery", "text": "Winery Husbandry Gold +500; Craft +5 "}, {"title": "Cidery", "url": "type-husbandry.html#cidery", "text": "Cidery Husbandry Gold +500; Craft +1; Faith +1 "}, {"title": "Mill", "url": "type-husbandry.html#mill", "text": "Mill Husbandry Gold +1000 "}, {"title": "Quarry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#quarry", "text": "Quarry Raw Materials Gold +500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Salt Works", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#salt-works", "text": "Salt Works Raw Materials Gold +500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Apiary", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#apiary", "text": "Apiary Raw Materials Gold +500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Peat Bog", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#peat-bog", "text": "Peat Bog Raw Materials Gold +500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Forestry", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#forestry", "text": "Forestry Raw Materials Gold +500; Craft +1 "}, {"title": "Fishmongery", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#fishmongery", "text": "Fishmongery Raw Materials Gold +500; Craft +2 "}, {"title": "Furnace", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#furnace", "text": "Furnace Raw Materials Gold +500; Unlocks Cast Weapons "}, {"title": "Common Land", "url": "type-raw-materials.html#common-land", "text": "Common Land Raw Materials Gold +1000; Doubt +1 "}, {"title": "Marshal Tiltyard", "url": "type-monument.html#marshal-tiltyard", "text": "Marshal Tiltyard Monument Initiative +1; Unlocks Lances regardless of Tier Unlock; Armies must be equipped with Lance "}, {"title": "Polish House", "url": "type-monument.html#polish-house", "text": "Polish House Monument Gold +3000; Craft +10; In the Envoy Phase, a player may target you with a Cunning Envoy. If they do, that Envoy gains Authority +1. If it Passes or is Endorsed, the action must target you "}, {"title": "Ossuary Crypt", "url": "type-monument.html#ossuary-crypt", "text": "Ossuary Crypt Monument All Piety actions that give Doubt give an additional Doubt +1; Immune Wavering Devotion "}, {"title": "Baggage Train", "url": "type-monument.html#baggage-train", "text": "Baggage Train Monument Supply -2000; At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may perform a Move action; Gain Immune Blocked "}, {"title": "Court Armoury", "url": "type-monument.html#court-armoury", "text": "Court Armoury Monument Supply -500; Planishing: Your to-Save can't be reduced beyond 10+; Unlocks Crafted Armor & Shield "}, {"title": "Serfdom", "url": "type-monument.html#serfdom", "text": "Serfdom Monument Build Timer -2; Gold +500 per Doubt "}, {"title": "Office of Works", "url": "type-monument.html#office-of-works", "text": "Office of Works Monument Siege Timer +2; Build Timer -2; Settlements & allied Armies inside them are not affected by 'Settlements being Besieged' restrictions "}, {"title": "Royal Pavilion", "url": "type-monument.html#royal-pavilion", "text": "Royal Pavilion Monument Armies gain Immune Strained; Improve Parry by +1; Deadly, & Cleave also trigger Focused Strikes on an Unmodified 8+ "}, {"title": "Imperial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#imperial-palace", "text": "Imperial Palace Monument If your Envoy would fail, it passes instead; Each Empire Phase, each non-allied player with a lower Prowess value gains Doubt +2 "}, {"title": "Artillery Park", "url": "type-monument.html#artillery-park", "text": "Artillery Park Monument Siege Timer -2; Siege Timers ignore Wooden & Stone Walls; Unlocks Arquebus; Settlements you Siege can't Sally Forth "}, {"title": "Ministry of Military Strategy", "url": "type-monument.html#ministry-of-military-strategy", "text": "Ministry of Military Strategy Monument Always gains Seize the Initiative, and your opponent doesn't; max initiative is increased to 3; Gain Drilled "}, {"title": "Thieves' Guild", "url": "type-monument.html#thieves-guild", "text": "Thieves' Guild Monument Whenever another player performs a Cunning action, you may recoup 1000 gold; Extort half of Trade Income from players who aren't your Trade Partners "}, {"title": "Senate Hall", "url": "type-monument.html#senate-hall", "text": "Senate Hall Monument Faith +1; Influence +1 per other player; In the Intrigue Phase, you may Condemn an At War player's Envoy or Endorse an Ally's Envoy "}, {"title": "Papal Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#papal-palace", "text": "Papal Palace Monument Each Empire Phase, Tithe each other player with lower Piety, resolved in the Extort step; You no longer pay cost for Piety Envoys "}, {"title": "Inquisitorial Palace", "url": "type-monument.html#inquisitorial-palace", "text": "Inquisitorial Palace Monument Doubt +1; Unlocks Grand Vizier which uses your Piety Value instead of Cunning; All player actions that cause Doubt are increased by 1 "}, {"title": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar", "url": "type-monument.html#preceptory-of-the-knight-s-templar", "text": "Preceptory of the Knight's Templar Monument While a Sacred War is active, gain 3 Faith during each Empire Phase; Unlocks Knight's Templar for Muster "}, {"title": "Exalted Basilica", "url": "type-monument.html#exalted-basilica", "text": "Exalted Basilica Monument Gold +300 per Faith; At the Start of the Empire Phase, you may perform an Endorsed Spread Truth "}, {"title": "Manor House", "url": "type-monument.html#manor-house", "text": "Manor House Monument Gold +200 per active Natural Holding "}, {"title": "Aristocratic Court", "url": "type-monument.html#aristocratic-court", "text": "Aristocratic Court Monument Whenever another player performs a Diplomacy action targeting another player, Extort 3000 from both players "}, {"title": "Studium Generale", "url": "type-monument.html#studium-generale", "text": "Studium Generale Monument Influence +1 per Established Standing; May gain one Sovereign Domain effect without spending the Domain Points "}, {"title": "Outlaw Rookery", "url": "type-monument.html#outlaw-rookery", "text": "Outlaw Rookery Monument Each Empire Phase, Extort the whole Treasury of every Bandit Camp within your Province; Bandit Camps and Armies within your Province don't target you and instead target another player at random "}, {"title": "Advanced Blast Furnace", "url": "type-monument.html#advanced-blast-furnace", "text": "Advanced Blast Furnace Monument Craft +5; Supply -1000; Unlocks Crafted Weapons "}, {"title": "Whispering Undercroft", "url": "type-monument.html#whispering-undercroft", "text": "Whispering Undercroft Monument In the Intrigue Phase, choose a Personal Envoy: its sender must declare the specific action & target they would Perform if it passes (including sub-Actions). If it passes, they must Perform that declared action at the declared target; You cast all of your votes in the Tally Phase "}, {"title": "Outrider Intercept Post", "url": "type-monument.html#outrider-intercept-post", "text": "Outrider Intercept Post Monument Every Skirmish, you may force your opponent to reveal their Tactic Card they selected before you select your own "}, {"title": "Port Authority", "url": "type-monument.html#port-authority", "text": "Port Authority Monument Craft +10; Gold +100 per Craft "}, {"title": "Turn Sequence", "url": "turn-sequence.html", "text": "turn sequence empire works diplomacy envoy battle rest phase order of play"}, {"title": "Dirt Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#dirt-roads", "text": "Dirt Roads infrastructure Can Trade; If you start a Move action within your Province, gain Speed +1"}, {"title": "Town Square", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#town-square", "text": "Town Square infrastructure Craft +2"}, {"title": "Muster Field", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#muster-field", "text": "Muster Field infrastructure Can Muster"}, {"title": "Wooden Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#wooden-walls", "text": "Wooden Walls infrastructure Siege Timer +1; Authority -2 on Raze actions from players targeting you; Authority -1 on Bandit Cunning actions targeting you"}, {"title": "Stone Roads", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#stone-roads", "text": "Stone Roads infrastructure If you start a Move action within your Province, gain additional Speed +2"}, {"title": "Town Hall", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#town-hall", "text": "Town Hall infrastructure Upkeep -500"}, {"title": "Garrison", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#garrison", "text": "Garrison infrastructure Each of your Settlements gains Muster Limit +5; Your Settlements gain Garrisons & Presence"}, {"title": "Stone Walls", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#stone-walls", "text": "Stone Walls infrastructure Siege Timer +1; Authority -2 on Destabilize actions from players targeting you; Authority -1 on Bandit Cunning actions targeting you"}, {"title": "March-Tower", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#march-tower", "text": "March-Tower infrastructure Instead of performing a Move action, you may have a Garrison Battle a Bandit Camp, Bandit Army, or an Army you're At War with within its Presence"}, {"title": "Bridges", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#bridges", "text": "Bridges infrastructure Armies cross Water Territory at full movement within your Province; Stone Roads may be built over Water"}, {"title": "Library", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#library", "text": "Library infrastructure Influence +2; Max Influence +1"}, {"title": "Chapel", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#chapel", "text": "Chapel infrastructure Faith +1"}, {"title": "Magistrate's Hall", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#magistrate-s-hall", "text": "Magistrate's Hall infrastructure Tax Income +1000 per Settlement"}, {"title": "Keep", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#keep", "text": "Keep infrastructure Siege Timer +1; When you Muster, reduce the Muster Timer by 1 and immediately gain Retinues equal to the combined muster limit; Your Settlement Wards have Presence"}, {"title": "Aqueducts", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#aqueducts", "text": "Aqueducts infrastructure Reach +2; Build Timer -1; Supply -1000; Upkeep -1000"}, {"title": "Cathedral", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#cathedral", "text": "Cathedral infrastructure Faith +1"}, {"title": "Colossus", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#colossus", "text": "Colossus infrastructure Speed +2; Siege Timer -2; Gain Immune Blunder; In the Intrigue Phase, you may support your own Personal Prowess Envoys before other players vote"}, {"title": "The Grand Exchange", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#the-grand-exchange", "text": "The Grand Exchange infrastructure You count as having 2 more Trade Partners. In addition, whenever you generate Trade Income from a Trade Partner, you generate twice as much for yourself"}, {"title": "The Eternal Sepulchre", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#the-eternal-sepulchre", "text": "The Eternal Sepulchre infrastructure If your Public Order would ever be less than 6, set it to 6 instead; Your Settlements gain Reach +2"}, {"title": "High Chancery", "url": "infrastructure-ref.html#high-chancery", "text": "High Chancery infrastructure Upkeep -2000; In the Tally Phase, you may Endorse one Envoy you sent"}, {"title": "Move", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Move Prowess action Move an Army up to its Speed in Territories. Then choose one: March \u2014 move up to 2\u00d7 Speed, lose 1 Endurance, take no other action; Battle \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Army not in a Settlement, then begin a Battle; Lay Siege \u2014 end adjacent to an at-war Settlement, then begin a Siege."}, {"title": "Declare War", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Declare War Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP or active truce with. You and that player are now At War, and any Trade Agreements between you end. If the target is in a Defensive Alliance, every member is now At War with you."}, {"title": "Pillage", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Pillage Prowess action Choose an army you control within Reach of an at-war player's Settlement without an active Siege Timer. While that army remains within Reach of that Settlement and does not Lay Siege, Battle, or March, it may Extort half of that Settlement's holding income in the Extort step. A Settlement may be Pillaged once per Empire Phase. Pillage ends if [war ends / army leaves Reach / Settlement is besieged]."}, {"title": "Muster", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Muster Prowess action Choose one: Raise \u2014 if you have fewer Armies than your Era allows, place a new Army within a Settlement under your Control; or Reinforce \u2014 choose an Army you control. The Army must be within range 2 of a Settlement you Control, while you have an active Muster Field, and at least Range 2 from any non-allied Army unless it is within Range 0 of a Settlement you Control. Choose how many Retinues to recruit (an Army can't exceed 25) and set a Muster Timer equal to that number \u00f7 your combined muster limit, rounded up. Each turn the Muster Timer counts down, the Army gains Retinues up to your combined muster limit and you begin paying their upkeep. You may change the Army's Retinue type and equipment while an army has an active Muster Timer. Reinforcing an Army that already has an active Muster Timer instead hurries it: reduce that Muster Timer by 1, and the Army gains Retinues up to your combined muster limit at once."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Demand Tribute Prowess action Choose a non-allied player you have no NAP with, then negotiate terms. If the target agrees, sign a NAP or Alliance (the target picks among the offered terms). If the target refuses, or later fails to meet the terms, immediately Declare War on them."}, {"title": "Intercept Caravan", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Intercept Caravan Cunning action Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose a player. The next turn that player is Host, Extort their Trade Income. If they have no Trade Income that turn, instead Extort 100 per their Craft."}, {"title": "Foster Rebellion", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Foster Rebellion Cunning action Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose a player. At the next Bandit Mechanics step, place a Bandit Camp of 10 Retinues in their Outlaw Country."}, {"title": "Raze", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Raze Cunning action Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose another player's Settlement, then choose one active Holding or active Infrastructure in it: it becomes Damaged, and its effects are inactive until Repaired. If you choose an active Build Timer in it instead, increase that Build Timer by 2."}, {"title": "Destabilize", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Destabilize Cunning action Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose a player. In the next Winter phase, during the Extort step, Extort one settlement's tax income. Each settlement can only be Destabilized once per Winter."}, {"title": "Sabotage", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sabotage Cunning action Extort 4000 from its target. Then, choose an army, that army gains Blocked."}, {"title": "Spread Truth", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Spread Truth Piety action Each non-allied player gains Doubt 1. Each allied player gains Faith 1."}, {"title": "Send Missionaries", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Send Missionaries Piety action Choose a target player or Alliance. If the target is outside your Alliance, each player in it gains Doubt 2. If the target is inside your Alliance, each other allied player gains Faith 2."}, {"title": "Tithe", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Tithe Piety action Choose a player. Extort 10% of their Treasury (round down to the nearest 100, minimum 0)."}, {"title": "Convert", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Convert Piety action Choose another player's closest non-capital Settlement; its Public Order must be -10 or lower. Lay Siege using only Settlement-type Siege modifiers (Settlement Size and Citadel) and set a Convert Timer. When it reaches 0, the Settlement joins your empire (see Capture)."}, {"title": "Sacred War", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sacred War Piety action Declare War on a non-ally you have no NAP or truce with, then immediately perform a Move action with one of your Armies."}, {"title": "Improve", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Improve Industry action Choose an unlocked, available Infrastructure and set a Build Timer equal to its build time. When it completes, the Infrastructure becomes active in every Settlement in your Province."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Repair Industry action Choose a Damaged Holding or Infrastructure in a Settlement you control and set Repair Timer 1. When it reaches 0, choose one: Restore \u2014 reactivate it with all effects; Demolish \u2014 remove the Holding tile from your Empire Tableau."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Build Industry action Choose an inactive Settlement Ward you control, then choose a Holding with one complete line of its Mastery Chain under your control (and meet its other requirements) and set a Build Timer equal to its build time (usually 1). When it completes, place the Holding in an available Ward slot; its effect activates immediately."}, {"title": "Settle", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Settle Industry action Charter a new Village on Grassland in your Province or within the Presence of one of your Armies, range 2+ from Outlaw Country, and set a Build Timer 2."}, {"title": "Expand", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Expand Industry action Increase a Settlement by one tier (Village to Town, Town to City, City to Metropolis), raising its Wards, Tax income, Muster Limit and Reach."}, {"title": "Sign Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Sign Treaty Diplomacy action Ask players to agree, then choose one and both sign it: Peace Treaty \u2014 end the war, set Truce Timer 5; Trade Agreement \u2014 begin trading next turn; Non-Aggression Pact \u2014 no Declare War (ending it via End Treaty gives both Truce Timer 5); Alliance \u2014 join, form, or invite to a Defensive or Military Alliance."}, {"title": "Negotiate", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "Negotiate Diplomacy action Propose terms to a target; they agree or refuse. Terms may include gold, Settlement ownership, Territory, signing or ending a Treaty, or promises (non-binding)."}, {"title": "End Treaty", "url": "actions-ref.html", "text": "End Treaty Diplomacy action Choose a target with whom you have an active Treaty and no active Truce Timer; remove that Treaty. The target doesn't need to agree."}, {"title": "Envoy Outcomes", "url": "envoy-outcomes-ref.html", "text": "envoy outcomes condemned failed passed endorsed net influence resolve domain"}, {"title": "Peace Treaty", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Peace Treaty treaty Ends war between the two players; sets Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Trade Agreement", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Trade Agreement treaty Begin trading (Trade Income flows from next turn). Requires active Dirt Roads or a Can Trade effect for each player."}, {"title": "Non-Aggression Pact", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Non-Aggression Pact treaty Neither player may Declare War on the other. Ending it via End Treaty gives both a Truce Timer 5."}, {"title": "Military Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Military Alliance treaty Mutual offensive pact: if a member Declares War, all members Declare War on the target next turn (and send 1 fewer envoy)."}, {"title": "Defensive Alliance", "url": "treaties-ref.html", "text": "Defensive Alliance treaty Mutual defense: attacking one member puts all members at war with the attacker."}, {"title": "Sovereign Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Sovereign Standing edict win Reach a Sovereign Standing (Domain value 10) in any Domain."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Monument edict win Have a Monument holding."}, {"title": "Wonder", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wonder edict win Complete a Wondrous Infrastructure."}, {"title": "Wealth", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Wealth edict win Hold 50,000 gold in your Treasury for five consecutive turns."}, {"title": "Vassalize", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Vassalize edict win Vassalize a rival player (control their capital with no other settlements/armies under them)."}, {"title": "Living Saints", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Living Saints edict win Sustain Public Order 10 (Living Saints) for five consecutive turns (Pious Timer)."}, {"title": "Last Alliance Standing", "url": "edicts-ref.html", "text": "Last Alliance Standing edict win Be the last alliance standing \u2014 the game-ending stop condition."}, {"title": "Economy Reference", "url": "economy-ref.html", "text": "upkeep costs pursuit army infrastructure tax trade 2000 gold (the Envoy action; the Holding then pays Holding upkeep each Empire Phase) Each Empire Phase: by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 0), Rising 200 (Build Timer 1), Established 300 (Build Timer 2), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 3); Natural 0 sum of each Army's cost (by Retinue type) - Supply -X modifiers Per-settlement (see INFRASTRUCTURE); Masonry removes Primitive, Trade Guild removes Developed, College of Engineering removes Sophisticated Raze the top-most Holding of each Ward; Extort 2000 per settlement tier; reduce settlement by 1 tier; the controller removes one Ward (sacker's choice) and its Holdings; Sack Timer 2 Winter tax by Settlement tier: Hamlet 0 / Village 2000 / Town 4000 / City 6000 / Metropolis 8000 100 x host's Craft X per active Trade Agreement 2000 gold (Intercept Caravan / Foster Rebellion / Raze / Destabilize / Sabotage) 2000 gold (Improve / Build / Settle / Expand); 0 gold (Repair) Doubt 1 (Spread Truth / Send Missionaries / Tithe / Convert / Sacred War) None (Move / Declare War / Pillage / Muster / Demand Tribute) None (Sign Treaty / Negotiate / End Treaty)"}, {"title": "Grassland", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Grassland terrain Where Settlements can be chartered (a Hill counts)."}, {"title": "Wetlands", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Wetlands terrain Speed -1 per Territory moved through"}, {"title": "Tundra", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Tundra terrain gain Strained"}, {"title": "Mountains", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Mountains terrain Impassable"}, {"title": "Water", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Water terrain Must end move after moving over 1 Water Territory (must end on land)"}, {"title": "Forest", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Forest terrain Speed -1 per Territory moved through"}, {"title": "Hill", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "Hill terrain Gains Seize the Initiative."}, {"title": "Terrain & Movement", "url": "terrain-ref.html", "text": "terrain movement grassland wetland barrens tundra mountain water forest roads bridge"}, {"title": "Bandits", "url": "bandits-ref.html", "text": "bandits outlaw country camp army growth cunning raze destabilize"}, {"title": "Timers, Influence & PO", "url": "systems-ref.html", "text": "timers influence public order modifiers faith doubt border tension"}, {"title": "Settlements", "url": "settlements-ref.html", "text": "settlements hamlet village town city metropolis tax muster wards reach"}, {"title": "Eras", "url": "eras-ref.html", "text": "eras founding ascension eminence zenith renown army cap"}, {"title": "Public Order Track", "url": "public-order-ref.html", "text": "public order faith doubt uprising living saints"}, {"title": "Domain Board", "url": "domain-board-ref.html", "text": "domain board standing indomitable grand vizier influence"}, {"title": "Seasons", "url": "seasons-ref.html", "text": "seasons winter spring summer fall"}, {"title": "Equipment", "url": "equipment-ref.html", "text": "equipment retinues weapons ranged shields armor stats"}, {"title": "Reference Tables", "url": "reference-tables.html", "text": "bandits timers influence gain trade rules build timers tier unlock standing effects"}, {"title": "Tactic Matrix", "url": "tactic-matrix-ref.html", "text": "tactic matrix scout ambush flank charge fighting defensive formation fall back initiative"}, {"title": "Escalation Campaign", "url": "escalation.html", "text": "escalation campaign combat battle mode overview"}, {"title": "Escalation Battle Rules", "url": "escalation-rules.html", "text": "escalation battle rules setup turn sequence skirmish walkthrough victory points dice"}, {"title": "Escalation Combat Pursuits", "url": "escalation-pursuits.html", "text": "escalation combat pursuits industry prowess piety cunning ranks mastery monument"}, {"title": "Combat Keywords", "url": "keywords-ref.html", "text": "keywords deadly cleave poison parry riposte"}, {"title": "Unbreakable", "url": "glossary.html#unbreakable", "text": "Unbreakable Skips the Break check entirely while Fatigued: never rolls, never takes break casualties. BUT still Routs if the morale target climbs to ROUT_THR+ from accumulated Fatigue. Stands fully immune, then collapses all at once \u2014 and because it stays full-size up to the Rout, it loses MORE soldiers when it finally breaks than a unit that bled down gradually."}, {"title": "Unshakable", "url": "glossary.html#unshakable", "text": "Unshakable Caps the morale target at CAP_THR permanently. Still TAKES every Break and Panic check each Skirmish (keeps bleeding casualties at a CAP_THR+ roll), but the target can never reach ROUT_THR, so it NEVER Routs. Bends and bleeds forever, never shatters. Makes the `shaking` stat (and the Abbey bonus) irrelevant \u2014 it's capped regardless."}, {"title": "Rally", "url": "glossary.html#rally", "text": "Rally Auto-passes the FIRST Break check it is ever required to take in a battle (no roll, no casualties, no Rout); every Break check after is normal. One free crisis, then mortal. The only one of the four that keeps `shaking` a live dial \u2014 so it's the one that synergizes with lowering KT base shaking and stacking Abbey +1."}, {"title": "Zealot", "url": "glossary.html#zealot", "text": "Zealot Locks the morale target at base `shaking`, ignoring ALL modifiers: Fatigue tokens don't raise it, shake bonuses (Abbey) don't lower it. Takes checks every Skirmish at that fixed number, never escalates, never Routs. A fixed wall whose strength is entirely its base stat. Unlike Unshakable (caps at 6), Zealot pins at base \u2014 which can be better or worse than 6 \u2014 and deliberately ignores Abbey synergy."}, {"title": "Steady", "url": "glossary.html#steady", "text": "Steady Initiative cannot be reduced by Tactics."}, {"title": "Unwieldy", "url": "glossary.html#unwieldy", "text": "Unwieldy Initiative cannot be improved by Tactics."}, {"title": "2H", "url": "glossary.html#2h", "text": "2H Cannot use a Shield: while a 2H weapon is Equipped, your Shield gives nothing that Skirmish (no Save bonus, Initiative or keywords)."}, {"title": "Deadly", "url": "glossary.html#deadly", "text": "Deadly On a Focused Strike: that Strike's AP is increased by 5, and the defender may Parry or Recover only with a Focused roll."}, {"title": "Unstoppable", "url": "glossary.html#unstoppable", "text": "Unstoppable -2 to the defender's Parry roll (to a maximum of 10+); a Parry against it can't Riposte."}, {"title": "Cleave", "url": "glossary.html#cleave", "text": "Cleave On a Focused Strike: roll one extra Strike die at your modified to-Strike."}, {"title": "Poison", "url": "glossary.html#poison", "text": "Poison When the Defender receives a Strike and rolls a Focused Save, it fails; the resulting wound may only be Recovered with a Focused Recover."}, {"title": "Nimble", "url": "glossary.html#nimble", "text": "Nimble Gain Initiative +1 in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Drilled", "url": "glossary.html#drilled", "text": "Drilled Does not lose Endurance in the first Skirmish of each Battle."}, {"title": "Destroy Shield", "url": "glossary.html#destroy-shield", "text": "Destroy Shield On a Focused Strike: the target loses its Shield attributes for the rest of the Battle."}, {"title": "Blunder", "url": "glossary.html#blunder", "text": "Blunder At Initiative -2, your to-Strike is set to 10+, before other negative modifiers."}, {"title": "One-Shot", "url": "glossary.html#one-shot", "text": "One-Shot Must be Equipped in the first Skirmish of a Battle, and can't be Equipped after it. Requires a Skirmish Field."}, {"title": "Parry", "url": "glossary.html#parry", "text": "Parry If your Army has gained Parry, roll a D10 to attempt to Parry a Strike before an Armor Save. On an 8+ (better with Improve Parry), the Strike is Parried and has no further effect."}, {"title": "Riposte", "url": "glossary.html#riposte", "text": "Riposte If your Army has gained Riposte and rolls a Focused Parry against a Melee Weapon's Strike, you Riposte: your opponent immediately takes a Strike from your melee weapon. You can Riposte a Riposte."}, {"title": "Awkward", "url": "glossary.html#awkward", "text": "Awkward While Equipped with this weapon during a Skirmish, you cannot Parry, and so cannot Riposte."}, {"title": "Recover", "url": "glossary.html#recover", "text": "Recover If your Army has gained Recover and a to-Save roll fails, roll a D10 & compare it to your Recover value: a result greater than or equal to your Recover value recovers the Retinue. Recovered Strikes still count toward the Panic check threshold."}, {"title": "Enduring", "url": "glossary.html#enduring", "text": "Enduring Successfully Recovered Strikes don't count toward the Panic check threshold."}, {"title": "Serrated", "url": "glossary.html#serrated", "text": "Serrated A cumulative -2 penalty to the defender's Recover roll."}, {"title": "Planishing", "url": "glossary.html#planishing", "text": "Planishing A Focused Save succeeds, regardless of AP."}, {"title": "Fatigue Token", "url": "glossary.html#fatigue-token", "text": "Fatigue Token Each token reduces Morale by 2; if your modified Morale is ever 11+, your Army Routs. Tokens stack."}, {"title": "Shielded", "url": "glossary.html#shielded", "text": "Shielded A cumulative -1 penalty to the Strike roll (to a maximum of 10+). Sources: a shield's -1 to Strike."}, {"title": "Dual Wield", "url": "glossary.html#dual-wield", "text": "Dual Wield A failed Strike is rerolled once; the rerolled Strike can be Focused. Dual Wield confers Two-Handed. You cannot reroll successful Strikes."}, {"title": "Florentine", "url": "glossary.html#florentine", "text": "Florentine Your Armies may equip two of the same 1H Melee Weapon to gain Dual Wield. While Dual Wielding, your Army gains Parry."}, {"title": "Immune [keyword]", "url": "glossary.html#immune-keyword", "text": "Immune [keyword] Can't gain that keyword's effect as it applies to your Army (e.g. Immune Strained, Destroy Shield, Steady, etc.)."}, {"title": "Negate [keyword]", "url": "glossary.html#negate-keyword", "text": "Negate [keyword] Your opponent can't gain that keyword's effect as it applies to their Army (e.g. Negate Shielded)."}, {"title": "AP", "url": "glossary.html#ap", "text": "AP Armor Penetration \u2014 a weapon's (negative) modifier to the defender's Save roll; the more negative, the harder to save."}, {"title": "Blocked", "url": "glossary.html#blocked", "text": "Blocked The next Move action this Army Performs fails, and then it loses Blocked. (An Army with Immune Blocked never gains it.)"}, {"title": "Strained", "url": "glossary.html#strained", "text": "Strained Initiative -1 every Skirmish (negated by Immune Strained). Does not gain Endurance in the Empire Phase."}, {"title": "Seize the Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#seize-the-initiative", "text": "Seize the Initiative Initiative +1 in the first Skirmish. The player who performed the Battle action usually has it; Terrain and the Ministry of Military Strategy can change that."}, {"title": "Attacker / Defender", "url": "glossary.html#attacker-defender", "text": "Attacker / Defender The Attacker performed the Move action that caused the Battle or Lay Siege; the other side is the Defender."}, {"title": "Battle", "url": "glossary.html#battle", "text": "Battle A collection of Skirmishes between two players, continuing until a side's Retinue count is reduced to 0, Routs, or successfully Falls Back, ending the Battle."}, {"title": "Skirmish", "url": "glossary.html#skirmish", "text": "Skirmish One round of a Battle, run through the numbered Battle steps; a Battle repeats Skirmishes until it ends."}, {"title": "Casualty", "url": "glossary.html#casualty", "text": "Casualty A Retinue removed from the Field \u2014 from an unsaved Strike or a failed Panic or Break check."}, {"title": "Field", "url": "glossary.html#field", "text": "Field Your Retinues in play \u2014 front line (up to 10) plus reserve (up to 5). Casualties leave the field at once, lowering its count."}, {"title": "Endurance", "url": "glossary.html#endurance", "text": "Endurance A side's stamina. Each side that fights loses 1 per Skirmish; at 0 it becomes Fatigued."}, {"title": "Fatigued", "url": "glossary.html#fatigued", "text": "Fatigued A side at 0 Endurance. Each Skirmish its Field takes a Break check, then it gains a Fatigue Token."}, {"title": "Break check", "url": "glossary.html#break-check", "text": "Break check Taken by each Fatigued side's Field every Skirmish, just before it gains its Fatigue Token. Roll Morale (5 dice, modified by Fatigue Tokens); failures are Casualties, but a Break check never triggers a Panic check. Unbreakable auto-passes."}, {"title": "Panic check", "url": "glossary.html#panic-check", "text": "Panic check Taken at most once per Skirmish by a side that suffered more than 5 Casualties in that Skirmish (Recovered Strikes count, unless Enduring), after both sides have Struck. Roll Morale (5 dice); Immune Panic auto-passes."}, {"title": "Morale", "url": "glossary.html#morale", "text": "Morale How steady a Retinue is when tested (lower is steadier; see the Retinue table). Break and Panic checks roll it: a D10 per Retinue in the Field, up to 5 dice, each must meet its modified value; failures are Casualties. If the modified value is ever 11+, the Army Routs."}, {"title": "Rout", "url": "glossary.html#rout", "text": "Rout The Army breaks and leaves the Battle. Apply Casualties equal to the remaining Retinues. Whenever an Army's modified Morale value reaches 11+, it Routs automatically."}, {"title": "Fall Back", "url": "glossary.html#fall-back", "text": "Fall Back A controlled retreat that ends the Battle with at least one Retinue left \u2014 a partial success."}, {"title": "Strike", "url": "glossary.html#strike", "text": "Strike A landed hit. Roll a D10, apply modifiers to the roll, and Strike on a Modified roll >= the to-Strike number. The target may then Parry, Save, and Recover."}, {"title": "to-Strike number", "url": "glossary.html#to-strike-number", "text": "to-Strike number The D10 result a Retinue needs to Strike (see the Retinue table; lower is better). Bonuses add to the roll; penalties and Fatigue Tokens subtract."}, {"title": "Save", "url": "glossary.html#save", "text": "Save The defender's roll to avoid a Casualty: roll a D10, add the weapon's AP (a negative) and the shield's Save bonus (a positive); the hit is saved on a Modified roll >= the armor value."}, {"title": "Unmodified roll", "url": "glossary.html#unmodified-roll", "text": "Unmodified roll The number on the die before any modifiers. Modifiers never change what counts as Unmodified."}, {"title": "Modified roll", "url": "glossary.html#modified-roll", "text": "Modified roll The number on the die after every modifier is applied."}, {"title": "Initiative", "url": "glossary.html#initiative", "text": "Initiative Decides who Strikes first each Skirmish (higher first). Runs -2 to +2 (Ministry can raise the maximum to +3). At -2 or lower you Blunder."}, {"title": "Tactic", "url": "glossary.html#tactic", "text": "Tactic A choice both players make secretly and reveal together each Skirmish; it can shift Initiative, Strike, and Save rolls."}, {"title": "Dual-equip", "url": "glossary.html#dual-equip", "text": "Dual-equip Carry two weapons at once (e.g. melee + ranged). Granted by the Skirmish Field."}, {"title": "Monument", "url": "glossary.html#monument", "text": "Monument A Domain's capstone Holding, one per game. Having one completes the Monument Edict."}, {"title": "Faith X", "url": "glossary.html#faith-x", "text": "Faith X Gain X Faith: each Faith raises your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Doubt X", "url": "glossary.html#doubt-x", "text": "Doubt X Gain X Doubt: each Doubt lowers your Public Order track by 1 when resolved."}, {"title": "Extort X", "url": "glossary.html#extort-x", "text": "Extort X Take X from the stated source: the gold goes to you instead of its owner."}, {"title": "Recoup X", "url": "glossary.html#recoup-x", "text": "Recoup X Undo up to X of the cost you paid (refund gold, or remove Doubt gained)."}, {"title": "Influence", "url": "glossary.html#influence", "text": "Influence The political currency: spend it to Support or Oppose Envoys. You gain it each Empire Phase from your Era, Trade Partners, Alliances, war, Holdings and Infrastructure. Influence +X gives X tokens in the Empire Phase unless it names another time."}, {"title": "Authority X", "url": "glossary.html#authority-x", "text": "Authority X An automatic change to an Envoy's Authority from a Holding, Infrastructure or Faction, applied while it's sent and resolved (once the action and target are chosen, if it depends on them)."}, {"title": "Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#envoy", "text": "Envoy Your means of acting: declare a Domain and spend 1 Envoy, and if it passes, choose and Perform an action of that Domain. Personal Envoys come from your Era (none in Spring)."}, {"title": "Vote", "url": "glossary.html#vote", "text": "Vote On each Envoy, every player except the sender, in clockwise order from the starting player, must Support, Oppose, or Abstain. No talking during a vote."}, {"title": "Support X", "url": "glossary.html#support-x", "text": "Support X Spend X Influence to increase an Envoy's Net Influence."}, {"title": "Oppose X", "url": "glossary.html#oppose-x", "text": "Oppose X Spend X Influence to decrease an Envoy's Net Influence."}, {"title": "Abstain", "url": "glossary.html#abstain", "text": "Abstain Decline to spend Influence on a Vote."}, {"title": "Council Phase", "url": "glossary.html#council-phase", "text": "Council Phase The phase after the Empire Phase: clockwise from the starting player, each player performs the Era's Works actions (Industry), paying each cost. They aren't Envoys: no Influence or votes, and each one Passes."}, {"title": "Intrigue Phase", "url": "glossary.html#intrigue-phase", "text": "Intrigue Phase The Envoy Phase step after the Forum, before the first Vote. No talking: the starting player uses all of their Intrigue Phase effects, then each player clockwise, ending with the Host. Each choice takes effect at once."}, {"title": "Tally Phase", "url": "glossary.html#tally-phase", "text": "Tally Phase The Envoy Phase step after every Envoy has been voted on: Supports, then the Votes of players who vote in the Tally Phase, then Endorsements, then effects that send another Envoy (voted at once). Resolve begins when it ends."}, {"title": "Personal Envoy", "url": "glossary.html#personal-envoy", "text": "Personal Envoy An Envoy you send in the Envoy Phase. How many you get, and how many actions each Performs, rise with the Era."}, {"title": "Settle", "url": "glossary.html#settle", "text": "Settle Found a new Village (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Expand", "url": "glossary.html#expand", "text": "Expand Raise a Settlement one tier: Village to Town, Town to City, City to Metropolis (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Muster", "url": "glossary.html#muster", "text": "Muster Raise a new Army or Reinforce an existing one near a Settlement you Control, while you have a Muster Field; Retinues arrive each Empire Phase over a Muster Timer (Prowess action)."}, {"title": "Build", "url": "glossary.html#build", "text": "Build Build a Holding, spending its purchase cost and a Settlement Ward (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Improve", "url": "glossary.html#improve", "text": "Improve Build Infrastructure, a Wonder included (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Repair", "url": "glossary.html#repair", "text": "Repair Restore a Damaged Holding or Infrastructure, or Demolish it (Industry action)."}, {"title": "Move", "url": "glossary.html#move", "text": "Move Advance an Army up to its Speed in Territories (Prowess action)."}, {"title": "Demand Tribute", "url": "glossary.html#demand-tribute", "text": "Demand Tribute Coerce gold or concessions from another player (Prowess action)."}, {"title": "Diplomacy", "url": "glossary.html#diplomacy", "text": "Diplomacy Sign Treaty, Negotiate and End Treaty: offers between players in the Diplomacy Phase (Spring's Envoy Phase, the only one each year), not sent as Envoys."}, {"title": "Treaty", "url": "glossary.html#treaty", "text": "Treaty A standing agreement between players (Trade Agreement, Non-Aggression Pact, Alliance), signed in the Diplomacy Phase."}, {"title": "Alliance", "url": "glossary.html#alliance", "text": "Alliance A Treaty binding players to mutual support; Military and Defensive Alliances unlock by Era."}, {"title": "Vassal", "url": "glossary.html#vassal", "text": "Vassal A player subordinated via Vassalization: their chartered Settlements return to them, they mirror the Suzerain's Treaties, count as allied to the Suzerain, and cannot Perform or be targeted by Diplomacy actions."}, {"title": "Suzerain", "url": "glossary.html#suzerain", "text": "Suzerain The player who has Vassalized another; the Vassal mirrors their Treaties."}, {"title": "Domain", "url": "glossary.html#domain", "text": "Domain One of the four Domains: Industry, Prowess, Cunning, Piety. Spend Domain Points to raise its value; the value sets your Standing there."}, {"title": "Domain Point", "url": "glossary.html#domain-point", "text": "Domain Point Gain 1 each Rest Phase; spend to raise a Domain value by 1."}, {"title": "Public Order", "url": "glossary.html#public-order", "text": "Public Order A track from -10 to 10, adjusted each turn by Faith minus Doubt; its band applies cumulative effects (see the Public Order table)."}, {"title": "Edict", "url": "glossary.html#edict", "text": "Edict A scoring achievement. Grants the Realm +1 Renown every time one is achieved."}, {"title": "Bandit", "url": "glossary.html#bandit", "text": "Bandit Neutral hostile force; Bandit Camps spawn in Outlaw Country and on low Public Order."}, {"title": "Outlaw Country", "url": "glossary.html#outlaw-country", "text": "Outlaw Country Uncontrollable Territory zones where Bandit Camps spawn (3 Territories each at Setup). A zone is your Outlaw Country while any of its Territories is within your Province. Foster Rebellion expands it when there is no room; otherwise, when there is no room, its Bandit Camps grow instead."}, {"title": "Wild Outlaw Country", "url": "glossary.html#wild-outlaw-country", "text": "Wild Outlaw Country Outlaw Country the Host places outside every Province at Setup. After Setup it works like any other Outlaw Country zone."}, {"title": "Siege", "url": "glossary.html#siege", "text": "Siege An Army holding Adjacent to an at-war Settlement while a Siege Timer counts down to Capture or Sack it."}, {"title": "Standing", "url": "glossary.html#standing", "text": "Standing How far you've risen in a Domain, set by its value: Untested, Rising (3+), Established (6+), Sovereign (10+). Each has a Standing Rank and its own Domain effects."}, {"title": "Max Influence", "url": "glossary.html#max-influence", "text": "Max Influence The most Influence you may spend to Support or Oppose on one Vote: your Standing Rank in that Domain. Max Influence +X raises it."}, {"title": "Standing Rank", "url": "glossary.html#standing-rank", "text": "Standing Rank Untested 1, Rising 2, Established 3, Sovereign 4. Your Envoys in a Domain start at Authority equal to your Standing Rank there; on each Vote in that Domain you may Support or Oppose up to your Standing Rank (your Max Influence)."}, {"title": "Border", "url": "glossary.html#border", "text": "Border You border a player when your Province is within or Adjacent to theirs."}, {"title": "Province", "url": "glossary.html#province", "text": "Province Every Territory your Settlements' Reach covers, Contested or not."}, {"title": "Region", "url": "glossary.html#region", "text": "Region A collection of Territories of the same Type."}, {"title": "Realm", "url": "glossary.html#realm", "text": "Realm The total collection of Regions."}, {"title": "Territory", "url": "glossary.html#territory", "text": "Territory 1 Hex."}, {"title": "Controlled", "url": "glossary.html#controlled", "text": "Controlled Territory that is within Reach of a Player's Settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Contested", "url": "glossary.html#contested", "text": "Contested Territory that is Controlled by more than one player's Settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Uncontested", "url": "glossary.html#uncontested", "text": "Uncontested Territory that is Controlled by a single Player's Settlement(s)."}, {"title": "Uncontrolled", "url": "glossary.html#uncontrolled", "text": "Uncontrolled Territory that is not within Reach of any Player Settlement."}, {"title": "Adjacent", "url": "glossary.html#adjacent", "text": "Adjacent Range 1."}, {"title": "Next to", "url": "glossary.html#next-to", "text": "Next to Range 2."}, {"title": "Within", "url": "glossary.html#within", "text": "Within Range 0."}, {"title": "Range X", "url": "glossary.html#range-x", "text": "Range X The amount of Territories you must move in order to get from your current position to the specific Territory."}, {"title": "Reach X", "url": "glossary.html#reach-x", "text": "Reach X How far a Settlement controls, set by its tier: every Territory within Range X of it is in your Province."}, {"title": "Host", "url": "glossary.html#host", "text": "Host Holds the Host Card; the starting player is the player directly clockwise from the Host, including in Spring. The role passes clockwise each Rest Phase (there is no Host in Spring). The Host collects and distributes Trade Income, resolves Bandit Mechanics, and breaks ties (Bandit targeting, and any tie not otherwise resolved)."}, {"title": "Targeting you", "url": "glossary.html#targeting-you", "text": "Targeting you An effect or action targeting you also targets what you own: your Settlements, Armies and Holdings."}, {"title": "Perform", "url": "glossary.html#perform", "text": "Perform When you Perform an action, immediately do the description of the action. Pay the action's normal Cost."}, {"title": "Resolve", "url": "glossary.html#resolve", "text": "Resolve Read an Envoy's Net Influence on the Envoy Resolution table and carry out the result."}, {"title": "Cost / Pay", "url": "glossary.html#cost-pay", "text": "Cost / Pay Cost to Perform an action, usually in Gold or Doubt."}, {"title": "Presence", "url": "glossary.html#presence", "text": "Presence Territory within Range 2 of a non-allied Army (Bandit Armies included, Bandit Camps not), or of a Settlement while its owner has a Garrison (and of its Settlement Wards while the owner has a Keep). An Army can't move within a non-allied Presence unless that Move Performs a Battle against it; a Battle or Lay Siege against a Settlement may pass through the Presence of that Settlement and its Wards."}, {"title": "Can Trade", "url": "glossary.html#can-trade", "text": "Can Trade You may take part in trade without active Dirt Roads (you still need a signed Trade Agreement)."}, {"title": "Net Influence", "url": "glossary.html#net-influence", "text": "Net Influence An Envoy's starting Influence (your Standing Rank) plus every Support, Oppose and Authority X. It sets the outcome: -4 or less Condemned, -3 to 0 Failed (gain Doubt 1), 1 to 3 Passed, 4+ Endorsed. Each Domain's result per outcome is in the Envoy Outcome table."}, {"title": "Condemned", "url": "glossary.html#condemned", "text": "Condemned Net Authority -4 or less."}, {"title": "Failed", "url": "glossary.html#failed", "text": "Failed Net Authority -3 to 0."}, {"title": "Passed", "url": "glossary.html#passed", "text": "Passed Net Authority 1 to 3."}, {"title": "Endorsed", "url": "glossary.html#endorsed", "text": "Endorsed Net Authority 4+."}, {"title": "Focused", "url": "glossary.html#focused", "text": "Focused An Unmodified 10."}, {"title": "Sally Forth", "url": "glossary.html#sally-forth", "text": "Sally Forth While a Settlement you control is besieged and you have an Army or Garrison inside it, you may Sally Forth: Battle in the Battle Phase without performing an action."}, {"title": "Garrison", "url": "glossary.html#garrison", "text": "Garrison An Army that exists within each of your Settlements while you have the Garrison Infrastructure, sized by that Settlement's Garrison value (Village 10, Town 15, City 25, Metropolis 50 Retinues). Garrisons can't Perform actions or be targeted by actions, and may Sally Forth while their Settlement is under Siege. Garrisons have cost and Supply 0 and don't count toward your Army limit. All your Garrisons share the same Retinue type and equipment, and gain the benefits of all unlocked keywords that apply to your Armies."}, {"title": "War Weariness", "url": "glossary.html#war-weariness", "text": "War Weariness Doubt 1 each Empire Phase per consecutive Battle you've lost."}, {"title": "Wavering Devotion", "url": "glossary.html#wavering-devotion", "text": "Wavering Devotion While your Public Order is below 0, you can't send Piety Envoys."}, {"title": "Settlement Ward", "url": "glossary.html#settlement-ward", "text": "Settlement Ward A slot in a Settlement that holds one Holding; a Settlement has one Ward per tier (a Hamlet has 3 Wards, Natural Holdings only). Each Ward occupies a Territory within Range 1 of the Settlement."}, {"title": "Mastery Chain X", "url": "glossary.html#mastery-chain-x", "text": "Mastery Chain X On a Holding tile: placed in the same Settlement Ward as X (the Raw Material or Holding named on it), it shares that Ward instead of taking its own. See Mastery Chain."}, {"title": "Natural", "url": "glossary.html#natural", "text": "Natural A Holding property: it pays no Upkeep and may be built in a Hamlet."}, {"title": "Supply", "url": "glossary.html#supply", "text": "Supply Gold you pay each Empire Phase for your Armies: each Army's cost by Retinue type, minus every Supply -X (never below 0). Holdings and Infrastructure pay Upkeep instead."}, {"title": "Upkeep", "url": "glossary.html#upkeep", "text": "Upkeep Gold you pay each Empire Phase for your Holdings and Infrastructure. Holding Upkeep by Standing: Untested 100 (Build Timer 0), Rising 200 (Build Timer 1), Established 300 (Build Timer 2), Sovereign 400 (Build Timer 3); Natural 0; each Infrastructure lists its own. Nothing is paid while a piece is inactive (being built, Damaged, under Repair or Shuttered). Upkeep -X lowers the total, never below 0."}, {"title": "Craft", "url": "glossary.html#craft", "text": "Craft Your trade value, from every effect that gives Craft +X. For each active Trade Agreement, both players gain 100 \u00d7 the Host's Craft."}, {"title": "Mastery Chain", "url": "glossary.html#mastery-chain", "text": "Mastery Chain A Holding's Mastery Chain is the line of Holdings it builds from, usually running from a Raw Material up to a Monument. You may start building a Holding only while you control one complete line of its Mastery Chain, anywhere in your empire; this is checked only when you start it. A Holding placed in the same Settlement Ward as its immediate parent shares that Ward, and the chain can continue upward the same way. Each Holding carries at most one descendant in its Ward. (Core Principle 13.)"}, {"title": "Shuttered", "url": "glossary.html#shuttered", "text": "Shuttered A Holding or Infrastructure set inactive while you're Insolvent because its Upkeep went unpaid. It gives no effect and pays no Upkeep, but its Upkeep still counts toward what you owe. It's restored at any Income & Upkeep step where you can pay its Upkeep. If it becomes Damaged, it's no longer Shuttered."}, {"title": "Speed X", "url": "glossary.html#speed-x", "text": "Speed X An Army's movement in Territories per Move action. Base Speed is 5."}, {"title": "Pursuit", "url": "glossary.html#pursuit", "text": "Pursuit A building you Build into a Settlement Ward, or into its Mastery Chain parent's Ward. Its effect applies while it's active."}, {"title": "Retinue", "url": "glossary.html#retinue", "text": "Retinue A single unit within an Army, represented by a single die roll for Strikes, Saves, etc."}, {"title": "At War", "url": "glossary.html#at-war", "text": "At War Two players At War can't trade, and may Battle, Lay Siege on and Pillage each other."}, {"title": "Equipped", "url": "glossary.html#equipped", "text": "Equipped The weapon chosen for the Skirmish."}, {"title": "Build Timer", "url": "glossary.html#build-timer", "text": "Build Timer Turns until a Holding, Infrastructure or Settlement finishes building and becomes active."}, {"title": "Repair Timer", "url": "glossary.html#repair-timer", "text": "Repair Timer Turns until a Damaged piece is repaired and its effects return."}, {"title": "Truce Timer", "url": "glossary.html#truce-timer", "text": "Truce Timer Turns until a Truce ends; until then neither player may Declare War on the other or End a Treaty with them."}, {"title": "Siege Timer", "url": "glossary.html#siege-timer", "text": "Siege Timer Turns until a Siege resolves; it doesn't count down in Winter."}, {"title": "Muster Timer", "url": "glossary.html#muster-timer", "text": "Muster Timer Turns until a Muster completes; each turn it counts down, the Army gains Retinues up to the combined Muster Limit."}, {"title": "Sack Timer", "url": "glossary.html#sack-timer", "text": "Sack Timer Turns until the sacking Army may Move or Lay Siege again."}, {"title": "Capture Timer", "url": "glossary.html#capture-timer", "text": "Capture Timer Turns until a Captured Settlement comes under your Control."}, {"title": "Convert Timer", "url": "glossary.html#convert-timer", "text": "Convert Timer Turns until a Convert attempt resolves; it fails early if conditions change."}, {"title": "Crude", "url": "glossary.html#crude", "text": "Crude Crude equipment tier. Weapons: Farm Tools, Cudgel, Pitchfork; Ranged: Hunting Bow; Armor: Gambeson; Shield: Buckler Shield. Unlocked by: Animal Husbandry (armor & shield)."}, {"title": "Cast", "url": "glossary.html#cast", "text": "Cast Cast equipment tier. Weapons: Daggers, Short Sword, Spears; Ranged: Longbow; Armor: Leather; Shield: Targe Shield. Unlocked by: Furnace (weapons), Tannery (armor & shield)."}, {"title": "Wrought", "url": "glossary.html#wrought", "text": "Wrought Wrought equipment tier. Weapons: Arming Sword, Pike, Flail, Halberd, Battle Axe, Cavalry Spear; Ranged: Javelin; Armor: Chainmail; Shield: Kite Shield. Unlocked by: Blacksmith (weapons), Armory (armor & shield)."}, {"title": "Forged", "url": "glossary.html#forged", "text": "Forged Forged equipment tier. Weapons: Morningstar, Bastard Sword, 2HBastard, War Hammer, Lance; Ranged: Crossbow; Armor: Full Plate; Shield: Tower Shield. Unlocked by: Gilded Foundry (armor & shield), Forge (all)."}, {"title": "Tempered", "url": "glossary.html#tempered", "text": "Tempered Tempered equipment tier. Weapons: Estoc, Poleaxe; Ranged: Pilum; Armor: Gothic Plate; Shield: Heater Shield. Unlocked by: Court Armoury (armor & shield), Advanced Blast Furnace (weapons)."}, {"title": "Gunpowder", "url": "glossary.html#gunpowder", "text": "Gunpowder Gunpowder equipment: Arquebus. Unlocked by: Artillery Park, Fletchery."}, {"title": "Ranged Weapons", "url": "glossary.html#ranged-weapons", "text": "Ranged Weapons Ranged weapons: Hunting Bow (Crude), Longbow (Cast), Javelin (Wrought), Crossbow (Forged), Pilum (Tempered), Arquebus (Gunpowder). Unlocked by: Fletchery."}, {"title": "Root", "url": "glossary.html#root", "text": "Root A Holding with no Mastery Chain requirement: you may start it without controlling a parent. If it names a Mastery Chain parent, it may still share that Holding's Settlement Ward."}, {"title": "Renown", "url": "glossary.html#renown", "text": "Renown The shared progress track. Gain 1 per Rest Phase; thresholds raise the Era (Ascension 8, Eminence 18, Zenith 30)."}, {"title": "Era", "url": "glossary.html#era", "text": "Era The stage of the game, set by Renown: Founding, Ascension, Eminence, Zenith. It sets Envoys, Influence and other limits."}, {"title": "Season", "url": "glossary.html#season", "text": "Season Winter, Spring, Summer, Fall: one per turn, each with its own effect; the Rest Phase advances it."}, {"title": "Empire Phase", "url": "glossary.html#empire-phase", "text": "Empire Phase The first phase of the turn: Timers, Bandits, Influence and Envoys, income, Supply and Upkeep, then Public Order."}, {"title": "Envoy Phase", "url": "glossary.html#envoy-phase", "text": "Envoy Phase Every player sends their Envoys; they are voted on, then resolved Domain by Domain."}, {"title": "Battle Phase", "url": "glossary.html#battle-phase", "text": "Battle Phase Battles and Sieges begun this turn resolve."}, {"title": "Rest Phase", "url": "glossary.html#rest-phase", "text": "Rest Phase The end of the turn: discard unused Envoys and Influence, advance the Season, score Renown and a Domain Point, pass the Host."}, {"title": "Treasury", "url": "glossary.html#treasury", "text": "Treasury The gold you Control."}, {"title": "Insolvent", "url": "glossary.html#insolvent", "text": "Insolvent You couldn't cover a cost in full: pay what you can, disband Armies, then set buildings Shuttered. Build Timers halt. It ends once your Treasury is above 0 and you can pay everything you owe."}, {"title": "Bankrupt", "url": "glossary.html#bankrupt", "text": "Bankrupt Insolvent with nothing left to cut: your Treasury goes negative by the debt. You can't spend gold (no actions with a gold cost) or be Extorted, and Revenue pays the debt first. It ends when your Treasury reaches 0."}, {"title": "Trade Agreement", "url": "glossary.html#trade-agreement", "text": "Trade Agreement A Treaty that lets two players trade. While both can trade, each gets Trade Income each turn either of them is Host."}, {"title": "Trade Partner", "url": "glossary.html#trade-partner", "text": "Trade Partner A player you have a Trade Agreement with and can trade with."}, {"title": "Settlement", "url": "glossary.html#settlement", "text": "Settlement A Village, Town, City or Metropolis (or your Hamlet). It earns Tax Income each Winter, holds Holdings in its Wards, has a Muster Limit, and controls Territory by its Reach."}, {"title": "Hamlet", "url": "glossary.html#hamlet", "text": "Hamlet Your farmland Settlement, placed at setup: no Tax Income or Muster Limit, 3 Wards for Natural Holdings only."}, {"title": "Army", "url": "glossary.html#army", "text": "Army Retinues on the map under your Control. Armies Move, Battle and Lay Siege, and pay Supply by Retinue type."}, {"title": "Infrastructure", "url": "glossary.html#infrastructure", "text": "Infrastructure An empire-wide building that applies to every Settlement you have. 5 tiers, Primitive to Wondrous; each needs one active Infrastructure of the tier below."}, {"title": "Wonder", "url": "glossary.html#wonder", "text": "Wonder Wondrous-tier Infrastructure, one per game. Several players may build the same Wonder; the first to finish takes it."}, {"title": "Damaged", "url": "glossary.html#damaged", "text": "Damaged A Holding or Infrastructure hit by Raze, Sack or Bandits: it has no effect and pays no Upkeep until Repaired."}, {"title": "Lay Siege", "url": "glossary.html#lay-siege", "text": "Lay Siege A Move that ends Adjacent to an at-war Settlement, starting its Siege Timer."}, {"title": "Capture", "url": "glossary.html#capture", "text": "Capture When a Siege resolves in your favor: set a Capture Timer; when it resolves, the Settlement comes under your Control."}, {"title": "Sack", "url": "glossary.html#sack", "text": "Sack When a Siege resolves in your favor: Damage the top Holding of each Ward, Extort 2000 per Settlement tier, reduce it one tier and remove one Ward."}, {"title": "Pillage", "url": "glossary.html#pillage", "text": "Pillage A Prowess action: while your Army stays within Reach of an at-war Settlement, it Extorts half of that Settlement's Holding income each Empire Phase, until it Battles, Lays Siege or Marches."}, {"title": "Diplomacy Phase", "url": "glossary.html#diplomacy-phase", "text": "Diplomacy Phase Spring's Envoy Phase: no Envoys are sent; players make Diplomacy offers to one another. The only time Diplomacy actions happen."}, {"title": "Map Generator", "url": "maps.html", "text": "map generator procedural board terrain hex seed rivers lakes resources start map"}, {"title": "Board Emulator", "url": "board.html", "text": "settlement board emulator pursuits wards infrastructure army public order renown domains"}, {"title": "The World of Vaelohk", "url": "lore.html", "text": "lore world vaelohk premise draggath fracture peoples"}, {"title": "The Map", "url": "lore-map.html", "text": "map vaelohk sea corners centre regions places geography duke unclaimed"}, {"title": "The Fifteen", "url": "lore-cultures.html", "text": "cultures fifteen Trusteki Ithiss Prezish Voldrastel Lenavorites Madekites Belvareth Shassolin Kraghs Vorghith Drakteni Cailendroffs Sarkopekt Astravantheliad Ossensteins"}, {"title": "The Timeline", "url": "lore-ages.html", "text": "timeline ages fracture plenty tetramorph doubt renown chronicle"}, {"title": "The Age of Darkness", "url": "lore-darkness.html", "text": "age of darkness old gods foundings draggath trusti clypso cailen"}];const q=document.getElementById('q'),box=document.getElementById('results');let sel=-1,cur=[];
q.addEventListener('input',()=>{const v=q.value.toLowerCase().trim();sel=-1;if(v.length<2){box.style.display='none';return;}
cur=IDX.map(d=>{const t=d.title.toLowerCase(),x=d.text.toLowerCase();let s=0;if(t===v)s=100;else if(t.startsWith(v))s=60;else if(t.includes(v))s=40;else if(x.includes(v))s=15;return{d,s};}).filter(o=>o.s>0).sort((a,b)=>b.s-a.s).slice(0,14);
if(!cur.length){box.innerHTML='<a><span class=s>No matches</span></a>';box.style.display='block';return;}
box.innerHTML=cur.map((o,i)=>`<a href="${o.d.url}" data-i="${i}"><span class="t">${o.d.title}</span> <span class="s">${o.d.text.slice(0,80).replace(/</g,'&lt;')}…</span></a>`).join('');box.style.display='block';});
q.addEventListener('keydown',e=>{const a=box.querySelectorAll('a');if(e.key==='ArrowDown')sel=Math.min(sel+1,a.length-1);else if(e.key==='ArrowUp')sel=Math.max(sel-1,0);else if(e.key==='Enter'&&cur.length){location.href=cur[Math.max(sel,0)].d.url;return;}else return;a.forEach((el,i)=>el.classList.toggle('sel',i===sel));e.preventDefault();});
document.addEventListener('click',e=>{if(e.target!==q)box.style.display='none';});